{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread","id":1400491,"title":"[V5] The official Sabbat speculation thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-02T03:23:08-07:00","id":1400491,"title":"[V5] The official Sabbat speculation thread","content":"This is the official forum thread for discussing the Sabbat in V5. With Justin Achilli having taken over as Creator Director and his handling of them in Revised, it's now entirely possible we may be seeing our old friends in the Sword of Caine return to a more prominent role in the setting.<br /> <br /> This is about speculating about their handling, their roles, and how to incorporate them when they come back from the Middle East or reveal they never entirely went in the first place.<br /> <br /> Also, how they will be handled with Paths and morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T03:50:15-07:00","id":1400492,"title":"","content":"right now, I'm wondering how the new diablerie mechanics will affect the plot,<br /> <br /> sabbat rely on diablerie for power, but now they can be overtaken by their victims,<br /> meaning that alot of the sabbat that survive will actually be Camarilla elders in a new body (no more elders being shorter than average I guess)<br /> <br /> if the vaulderie is still a thing, that would mean some of the camarilla that were stuck with a blood bond for centuries will finally be free, and thirsty for revenge,<br /> it's like the Anarch revolt all over again<br /> <br /> that's gonna be...weird<br /> <br /> paths are definitely gone, since they require some structure and stability to maintain,<br /> pathers will have a hard time reconciling their morality and vampire supremacism with their constant losses and lack of hierarchy,<br /> <br /> apart from path of the beast, I don't see what could survive","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 07-02-2020, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T04:40:27-07:00","id":1400493,"title":"","content":"Nothing really concrete to say, but really looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think they\u2019ll completely get rid of Paths, but I do think they might change the mechanics somewhat and maybe make it so only a few Sabbat ancillae and elders follow them.<br /> <br /> Cool! I forgot to capitalize Paths and my autocorrect did it for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T04:42:21-07:00","id":1400494,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. You raise a really good point about Diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T04:45:49-07:00","id":1400495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400494#post1400494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm. You raise a really good point about Diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, there's a serious question of how many vampires was a Sabbat vampire expected to commit diablerie against in their lifetime? Is it something that happens once or twice a lifetime or were people playing it as a regular thing in a Sabbat vampire's life?<br /> <br /> Do packs do diablerie as a group or as a single vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T04:50:10-07:00","id":1400497,"title":"","content":"I always felt like Diablerie was a rarity, a big event in a Sabbat Cainite\u2019s life when it happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T04:57:09-07:00","id":1400498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400497#post1400497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt like Diablerie was a rarity, a big event in a Sabbat Cainite\u2019s life when it happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It's why I never really thought it was a bad thing even for Road of Blood or Road of Caine people to have issues when they did it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, its a religious sacrament to eat souls. It's also going to screw with your brain.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T05:00:44-07:00","id":1400500,"title":"","content":"Exactly!<br /> <br /> Imma get up and start my day now. Happy gaming \ud83d\ude0a. Have a great day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T05:16:26-07:00","id":1400501,"title":"","content":"if you want to survive past the 10 year mark, you're gonna need diablerie,<br /> if you want any adavancement in the sect or a path or be any kind of leader, you're gonna need diablerie,<br /> you want to protect your freedom against elders and hunters, you're gonna need diablerie,<br /> you wanna survive monomacy, you're gonna need diablerie,<br /> you want to sire childer that won't turn out to be thin bloods, you're gonna need diablerie<br /> <br /> you can argue that, statistically, most sabbat don't diablerize,<br /> but also, statistically, most sabbat don't survive long<br /> <br /> here we're talking about the sabbat that are still around, the 1 in 10 that hasn't died during the gehenna crusade,<br /> the ones that matter, that will shape the future of the sect<br /> <br /> high gens don't build sects, certainly not sects that champion cainite supremacy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T06:30:46-07:00","id":1400509,"title":"","content":"Yes, but the Sabbat can really only commit Diablerie during sieges or crusades and those aren\u2019t that common. Also, when I said Diablerie was pretty rare, I was primarily thinking of Diablerie committed against elders. Very few rank and file Sabbat members will ever get the opportunity to Diablerize an elder, with or without the help of their pack.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> hmm. I wonder if that\u2019s why the Antediluvians didn\u2019t Diablerize the Second Generation. They knew the consequences of Diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T06:55:12-07:00","id":1400513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400509#post1400509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;12002&quot;] I wonder if that\u2019s why the Antediluvians didn\u2019t Diablerize the Second Generation. They knew the consequences of Diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>because:<br /> 1- diablerie wasn't known at the time, the first vampire to commit diablerie was an assamite on a toreador named amarantha (thus the name amaranth), neither were 3rd gen,<br /> 2- generation wasn't a thing either back then, since the curse that would make childer lose blood potency was only applied after the murdering of the 2nd gen<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but the Sabbat can really only commit Diablerie during sieges or crusades and those aren\u2019t that common. </div> </div> </div>no, they can diablerize other sabbat in monomacy, bloodhunt or turf war<br /> <br /> they can diablerize non-sabbat whenever they wish, if they can, same for anarchs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 07-02-2020, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T07:12:32-07:00","id":1400516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400495#post1400495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, there's a serious question of how many vampires was a Sabbat vampire expected to commit diablerie against in their lifetime? Is it something that happens once or twice a lifetime or were people playing it as a regular thing in a Sabbat vampire's life?<br /> <br /> Do packs do diablerie as a group or as a single vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> regularly, but getting a target of lower generation was rare. At least in my experience, most if not all Vampire on Vampire combats (not duels or position fights, Sabbat vs Anarch/Cam/Independent or Pack vs Pack wars) ended with the killing blow via Diablerie, the times that it didn't was because of aggravated damage dusting the target. But that is a playstyle thing I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T08:01:27-07:00","id":1400522,"title":"","content":"Yes, but I still think Diablerie is a rare occurrence even for the Sabbat, especially Diablerie of an elder. It just doesn\u2019t happen all the time in the average vampire\u2019s nightly existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T08:25:58-07:00","id":1400524,"title":"","content":"I think about one diablerie per pack a year sounds about right on average. Obviously it will vary wildly from pack to pack baised on where they are, how violent they are and what paths they are on, but that seems right to me.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, I've committed more diablerie in the Camarilla than the Sabbat...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T08:37:48-07:00","id":1400525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400524#post1400524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amusingly, I've committed more diablerie in the Camarilla than the Sabbat...</div> </div> </div> </div>bloodhunts or sect wars? (or neither?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T09:14:38-07:00","id":1400527,"title":"","content":"I've played more camarilla games, so it's only natural I've diablerised more with them (Sect wars) <br /> <br /> I just want to remind everyone that Diablerie works best when it's easy. Revised made diablerie an ordeal, something you don't want to do often. Something that you need to recover from. That's far less terrifying than the idea that anyone who tries it will want to do it more. The automatic humanity loss is a dumb idea; It causes players to avoid the practice. And then there's V5's Diablerie mechancs that... encourage high humanity vampires to diablerise while turning away low humanity vampire (and yeah, I guess for V5 you can kinda excuse it with the fact that whilst players might know the mechanics, characters don't, but it's still an abhorent system, especially when it potentially grants huge swaths of discipline XP to a player and fucks party power dynamics up) <br /> <br /> Is this the guy that added in that diablerie revision? <br /> <br /> Also, the more I'm learning about the occult ideologies behind VTM, the more 'WTF' I am to humanity being the one-true-way and diablerie being bad-wrong-never-do-it. Now, sure, maybe I shouldn't be taking advice from Setites and Tremere, but they're almost certainly right about a few things. God (The demiurge) is a bastard and reality is a prison in this setting; It doesn't make sense that 'humanity' and denying your vampiric nature should be the one true way. That's gothic, but it sure as hell ain't punk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T09:17:09-07:00","id":1400528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400525#post1400525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> bloodhunts or sect wars? (or neither?)</div> </div> </div> </div>They were Sabbat, one was due to s frenzy when they attacked elysium, the other, well, it might have been due to extorting the prince for a sanction...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T09:37:35-07:00","id":1400533,"title":"","content":"I'm running a retro '91 Sabbat V20 game right now with a nomadic pack of neonates and 3/4 of the players have succeeded in Diablerie. I'm mostly using the rules from the V20 Black Hand book for Diablerie, with options for permanent discipline transferrrence, but only going to do a chance for possession if the victim were really powerful and strong willed. Under the V20 rules, you needed to accumulate 7 successes on an extended strength roll at difficulty 9, so that's the only reason one of the players has failed their Diablerie. None of them started lower than 11th Gen and most were 13th, so finding someone with lower gen hasn't been much of an issue. They've been skulking around smaller towns and cities that aren't too heavily defended to achieve this. Nobody missed the pair of Autarkis hiding in Barstowe. So by keeping away from the centers of Camarilla power, they've managed to do the deed and get away with it. This is partially because of the group I'm dealing with. I wasn't comfortable making them more than neonates with the knowledge the players actually have about the Sabbat, but I wanted to get them leveled up fast so they can get to doing sieges in a bigger cities. They're a nomadic pack, so they're just a bunch of murder hobos, for me it makes complete sense for them to prey on the edges of kindred society. They also gang up on a lone vampire or two and ambush them or had the help from an older pack and take turns on performing the Amaranth. I'm curious to see how they deal with a single real elder Lasombra Antitribu in the next game or 2, I strongly suspect at least one or 2 are going to die. So yes, I think at least early on Diablerie could be fairly common by a nomadic pack of neonates, although a lot of them die in the process.<br /> <br /> Also packs can't commit Diablerie together. They can help each other take down a more powerful vampire, but only one can actually do the deed, at least by the V20 rules I'm using. I don't recall if that was changed in V5.<br /> <br /> Doing Diablerie in V5, they'd probably also have to make sure members that commit the Amaranth aren't possessed and undergo interrogation. Or here's just a thought, maybe there's a Ritus that could decrease the chances the diablerist gets possessed.<br /> <br /> Asides from Diablerie, I hope Montreal, Mexico City and other major areas in Central America are a trap for the Cam. Once they get settled in, Revanent families come out of the woodwork with help from the local police and army and drag a ton of Cammys that had moved in into the sun during the day or bomb their havens.<br /> <br /> After the surprise return, they'll try to make some incursions into Cam territory with great success initially killing the weakened Cammies. When things look really bad, though, they're pushed back into the central America not by the Cam, but by the Second Inquisition and take massive losses, balancing power structure again. This leads to the SI becoming aware that there are factions among vampires and some awareness as to how they differ.<br /> <br /> I think the younger ones will get disillusioned with the crusade in the middle east. Too many of them dying, the true faith emanating from Mecca and no success actually finding an Antedeluvian will disenchant the youth with the crusade and they'll return. The older ones are also affected by the Beckoning and stay behind to continue the fight in the middle east, which indisposes of the oldest on that side, too.<br /> <br /> I also want paths to return full force. You don't survive as a murder hobo for decades unless you're a psychopath or not trying to hang onto your humanity. They added such a unique flavor to the world. I'm not a fan of touchstones, but institutions or ideals as touchstones, seems like it'd be necessary for a Sabbat vampire since they don't maintain mortal connections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T10:18:37-07:00","id":1400538,"title":"","content":"one of my grievances in revised was willpower,<br /> there was not enough of it to deal with diablerie addiction<br /> <br /> from what I heard, they fixed that in V5 by making willpower more available, is it true?<br /> <br /> also wondering if you can spend willpower during diablerie in V5? (the rolls you make for each blood potency or whatnot)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400527#post1400527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the more I'm learning about the occult ideologies behind VTM, the more 'WTF' I am to humanity being the one-true-way and diablerie being bad-wrong-never-do-it. Now, sure, maybe I shouldn't be taking advice from Setites and Tremere, but they're almost certainly right about a few things. God (The demiurge) is a bastard and reality is a prison in this setting; It doesn't make sense that 'humanity' and denying your vampiric nature should be the one true way. That's gothic, but it sure as hell ain't punk.</div> </div> </div> </div>unfortunately, the demiurge was never made canon, it's always Yahweh, even in other splats,<br /> <br /> though, as far as I know, Phipps is wrong about humanity being the one true way (even in revised)<br /> even if it's the only way to gain Yahweh's favor, it didn't mean much since humanitas was just impossible to maintain at high levels,<br /> only vampires with true faith or extremely na\u00efve ones could,<br /> <br /> paths of enlightenement were desperate, but they offered more,<br /> they offered a reconciliation with your nature (instead of a constant conflict with it),<br /> and it also offered you to put your faith in other, more compelling, deities (Caine, Lilith, Demons, Demiurge, even Gaia and the Triat for some...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T10:25:50-07:00","id":1400540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400538#post1400538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of my grievances in revised was willpower,<br /> there was not enough of it to deal with diablerie addiction<br /> <br /> from what I heard, they fixed that in V5 by making willpower more available, is it true?<br /> <br /> also wondering if you can spend willpower during diablerie in V5? (the rolls you make for each blood potency or whatnot)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> unfortunately, the demiurge was never made canon, it's always Yahweh, even in other splats,<br /> <br /> though, as far as I know, Phipps is wrong about humanity being the one true way (even in revised)<br /> even if it's the only way to gain Yahweh's favor, it didn't mean much since humanitas was just impossible to maintain at high levels,<br /> only vampires with true faith or extremely na\u00efve ones could,<br /> <br /> paths of enlightenement were desperate, but they offered more,<br /> they offered a reconciliation with your nature (instead of a constant conflict with it),<br /> and it also offered you to put your faith in other, more compelling, deities (Caine, Lilith, Demons, Demiurge, even Gaia and the Triat for some...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised made Golconda canon with SINS OF THE BLOOD.<br /> <br /> It provided the rules and how it wa sachieved.<br /> <br /> Also, it can only be done with Humanity.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sins_of_the_Blood\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sins_of_the_Blood</a><br /> <br /> Justin Achilli was the developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T10:36:25-07:00","id":1400542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400527#post1400527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the more I'm learning about the occult ideologies behind VTM, the more 'WTF' I am to humanity being the one-true-way and diablerie being bad-wrong-never-do-it. Now, sure, maybe I shouldn't be taking advice from Setites and Tremere, but they're almost certainly right about a few things. God (The demiurge) is a bastard and reality is a prison in this setting; It doesn't make sense that 'humanity' and denying your vampiric nature should be the one true way. That's gothic, but it sure as hell ain't punk.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Church of Set is always accepting new converts\u2026just sayin'\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T10:41:23-07:00","id":1400544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400540#post1400540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revised made Golconda canon with SINS OF THE BLOOD.<br /> <br /> It provided the rules and how it wa sachieved.<br /> <br /> Also, it can only be done with Humanity.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sins_of_the_Blood\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sins_of_the_Blood</a><br /> <br /> Justin Achilli was the developer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but humanity was still a hard road, and few achieved salvation,<br /> <br /> chaining the beast was rather specific about it,<br /> and high humanity vampires were negatively perceived in both sects<br /> <br /> paths led nowhere, but they were still the logical choice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T11:07:10-07:00","id":1400546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400527#post1400527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played more camarilla games, so it's only natural I've diablerised more with them (Sect wars)<br /> <br /> I just want to remind everyone that Diablerie works best when it's easy. Revised made diablerie an ordeal, something you don't want to do often. Something that you need to recover from. That's far less terrifying than the idea that anyone who tries it will want to do it more. The automatic humanity loss is a dumb idea; It causes players to avoid the practice. And then there's V5's Diablerie mechancs that... encourage high humanity vampires to diablerise while turning away low humanity vampire (and yeah, I guess for V5 you can kinda excuse it with the fact that whilst players might know the mechanics, characters don't, but it's still an abhorent system, especially when it potentially grants huge swaths of discipline XP to a player and fucks party power dynamics up)</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like your mechanics for a game which has meth and heroin in it would be &quot;These should just give people superpowers because if not players won't use them&quot;. How do you balance that it is SUPPOSED To be addictive but also REALLY bad for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T11:18:47-07:00","id":1400547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400542#post1400542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Church of Set is always accepting new converts\u2026just sayin'\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>My player character is an Anarch following the Church of Caine. He hates the Setites because they're only right about 90% of reality! The remaining 10% is worth killing over.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T11:21:16-07:00","id":1400548,"title":"","content":"That's a shitty analogy.<br /> <br /> Diablerie isn't supposed to be bad for you? Socially, yeah, they'll kill you for it, but physically? It brings you closer to &quot;Caine&quot;, it literally makes your blood and soul stronger. You are returning to the strength of the primordial vampire, you are transending the limitations of earthly shackles, and you're killing an elder who probably deserved it. With all that in mind, maybe it's worth a gamble with humanity? But if you just took a huge hit everytime you did it, it would suck and you wouldn't do it again.<br /> <br /> RE: Heroin and other addictive substances<br /> You'd get willpower for doing it and roll willpower to resist the temptation of doing it more. Perhaps a stamina/Medicine roll would be there to keep you from killing yourself. The first part probably could help provide mechanics for diablerie addiction, but people don't get addicted after only one shot of heroin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T11:29:54-07:00","id":1400551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400548#post1400548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a shitty analogy.<br /> <br /> Diablerie isn't supposed to be bad for you? Socially, yeah, they'll kill you for it, but physically? It brings you closer to &quot;Caine&quot;, it literally makes your blood and soul stronger. You are returning to the strength of the primordial vampire, you are transending the limitations of earthly shackles, and you're killing an elder who probably deserved it. With all that in mind, maybe it's worth a gamble with humanity? But if you just took a huge hit everytime you did it, it would suck and you wouldn't do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is. Its not supposed to be good for you. Like Sith Philosophy the &quot;diablere is awesome&quot; is meant to be hollow. Its meant to be a lie. Its meant to justify a quick and dangerous path to power. The reason why every person on Golconda successfully leaves vampire society is because its a game you cannot win. Every move is just a different method of losing. Diablere's &quot;Loss&quot; condition is becoming someone's new body of a wight.<br /> <br /> Actually lets consider instead how many vampires become wights even without Diablere. How many vampires are expected to survive even a human life time much less bask in &quot;Immortality&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T11:47:50-07:00","id":1400553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400551#post1400551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it is. Its not supposed to be good for you. Like Sith Philosophy the &quot;diablere is awesome&quot; is meant to be hollow. Its meant to be a lie. Its meant to justify a quick and dangerous path to power. The reason why every person on Golconda successfully leaves vampire society is because its a game you cannot win. Every move is just a different method of losing. Diablere's &quot;Loss&quot; condition is becoming someone's new body of a wight.<br /> <br /> Actually lets consider instead how many vampires become wights even without Diablere. How many vampires are expected to survive even a human life time much less bask in &quot;Immortality&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think wight's wouldn't be too common. Losing those last few dots of humanity isn't that easy and staying alive when you're so obviously monstrous to even other kindred is going to be difficult, at least outside of the Sabbat, which is what paths were for. They make a fun little side quest when you just need to throw the party a quick track and kill/capture quest, though. Staying alive as a wight can't be that easy, either. Someone breaches their haven during the day, or even worse the SWAT team, combined with both the Camarilla and Sabbat wanting them dead or to use them doesn't make for a long life.<br /> <br /> My understanding was vampires actually had a pretty high mortality rate and most didn't make it past their first 10 years. A lot of them probably just screw up hunting at some point and get outnumbered and offed or piss off their sire or the other wrong person and they're written off as a mistake and burnt. Plus there's probably a sizeable chunk of the ones that died who just decide from the get go, they can't deal with the whole drinking blood to survive thing and just commit suicide in their first nights. It's a little like human mortality rates in the middle ages. Get through your childhood and you can live to a decent age","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T11:55:16-07:00","id":1400556,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1037_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1037\" data-vbnamecard=\"1037\">jamiemalk</a> I agree with your analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T12:01:08-07:00","id":1400557,"title":"","content":"The Demiurge (the idea of a blatantly evil God) is from Kult, not Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T12:21:16-07:00","id":1400561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400551#post1400551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it is. Its not supposed to be good for you. Like Sith Philosophy the &quot;diablere is awesome&quot; is meant to be hollow. Its meant to be a lie. Its meant to justify a quick and dangerous path to power. The reason why every person on Golconda successfully leaves vampire society is because its a game you cannot win. Every move is just a different method of losing. Diablere's &quot;Loss&quot; condition is becoming someone's new body of a wight.<br /> <br /> Actually lets consider instead how many vampires become wights even without Diablere. How many vampires are expected to survive even a human life time much less bask in &quot;Immortality&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Like jedi Philosophy the &quot;diablere is awful&quot; is meant to be hollow. Its meant to be a lie. Its meant to justify a static status quo where everyone knows their place; Some people are just better than others by matter of birth, and you should just lie down like a dog and accept that. Diablerie's loss condition is that you become the tasty next meal. <br /> <br /> Actually let's consider how many vampires are killed off by their despotic elders for imagined slights even without diablerie? How many vampires are expected to survive a human life time much less bask in &quot;Immortality&quot;</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T12:36:21-07:00","id":1400563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400561#post1400561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Like jedi Philosophy the &quot;diablere is awful&quot; is meant to be hollow. Its meant to be a lie. Its meant to justify a static status quo where everyone knows their place; Some people are just better than others by matter of birth, and you should just lie down like a dog and accept that. Diablerie's loss condition is that you become the tasty next meal.<br /> <br /> Actually let's consider how many vampires are killed off by their despotic elders for imagined slights even without diablerie? How many vampires are expected to survive a human life time much less bask in &quot;Immortality&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Diablerie's downsides aren't a matter of morality. Just the fact that eating someone's soul will fuck you up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T12:43:40-07:00","id":1400565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400501#post1400501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you want to survive past the 10 year mark, you're gonna need diablerie,<br /> if you want any adavancement in the sect or a path or be any kind of leader, you're gonna need diablerie,<br /> you want to protect your freedom against elders and hunters, you're gonna need diablerie,<br /> you wanna survive monomacy, you're gonna need diablerie,<br /> you want to sire childer that won't turn out to be thin bloods, you're gonna need diablerie, high gens don't build sects, certainly not sects that champion cainite supremacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, correct on all counts. If there's one lesson that a neonate needs to learn before all other things about kindred society, it is this: Mediocrity is your greatest enemy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","user":"Gangrel44","date":". 07-02-2020, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T13:00:22-07:00","id":1400566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400563#post1400563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Diablerie's downsides aren't a matter of morality. Just the fact that eating someone's soul will fuck you up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You sure they're not just returned to the cycle after digestion? Even if trapped, would such a soul feel it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T13:12:43-07:00","id":1400569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400566#post1400566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You sure they're not just returned to the cycle after digestion? Even if trapped, would such a soul feel it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The beast devours it whole, kinda like how an amoeba eats another one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T13:18:54-07:00","id":1400572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400566#post1400566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You sure they're not just returned to the cycle after digestion? Even if trapped, would such a soul feel it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends on how you want to roleplay it. My view is the soul is entrapped inside the vampire and will remain there until the vampire meets the Final Death, lingering in the back of their mind. Its the reason that they can potentially learn new Disciplines and possibly gain new Skills they might other. I don't think that Monty Coven should be normal and I don't think that anyone without a botch on a willpower roll should be &quot;possessed&quot; by a soul. Mithras and Monty was a once-in-a-millennium thing, though I suppose more could happen in the Middle East because so many ancients are coming out of torpor.<br /> <br /> I basically use diablerie like Highlander (which is good because that was a big influence on V:TM 1st Edition). You absorb their essence but very rarely is it going to do more than make you more powerful.<br /> <br /> If you fail, you should maybe get a personality change or minor element of the person you've eaten like a sudden interest in baseball or finance or maybe start feeling guilt you haven't felt for killing humans you haven't felt in centuries.<br /> <br /> Not, &quot;And now Bob is Lodin.&quot;<br /> <br /> I admit I sometimes do have the voices of a diablerized soul whisper to the people who killed them but that's because it's a horror game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T13:25:17-07:00","id":1400574,"title":"","content":"I expect the &quot;new&quot; Sabbat to be something like 7 in VtR, a mysterious sect striking from the Shadows, killing, subverting and generally causing mayhem.<br /> <br /> The conflict between the Anarchs and the Camarilla is political. The Sabbat needs to give the game something different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T13:27:50-07:00","id":1400575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400572#post1400572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose it depends on how you want to roleplay it. My view is the soul is entrapped inside the vampire and will remain there until the vampire meets the Final Death, lingering in the back of their mind. Its the reason that they can potentially learn new Disciplines and possibly gain new Skills they might other. I don't think that Monty Coven should be normal and I don't think that anyone without a botch on a willpower roll should be &quot;possessed&quot; by a soul. Mithras and Monty was a once-in-a-millennium thing, though I suppose more could happen in the Middle East because so many ancients are coming out of torpor.<br /> <br /> I basically use diablerie like Highlander (which is good because that was a big influence on V:TM 1st Edition). You absorb their essence but very rarely is it going to do more than make you more powerful.<br /> <br /> If you fail, you should maybe get a personality change or minor element of the person you've eaten like a sudden interest in baseball or finance or maybe start feeling guilt you haven't felt for killing humans you haven't felt in centuries.<br /> <br /> Not, &quot;And now Bob is Lodin.&quot;<br /> <br /> I admit I sometimes do have the voices of a diablerized soul whisper to the people who killed them but that's because it's a horror game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much like how I run Diablerie. Possession should be for only when the victim's extremely powerful and strong willed and there's a huge gap in power between the victim and the diablerist. The fact is it's kind of a dick move to take away free will from the player. In small doeses of presence and dominate, that's fine, but just yanking someone's character away from them is harsh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T15:10:54-07:00","id":1400586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400574#post1400574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect the &quot;new&quot; Sabbat to be something like 7 in VtR, a mysterious sect striking from the Shadows, killing, subverting and generally causing mayhem.<br /> <br /> The conflict between the Anarchs and the Camarilla is political. The Sabbat needs to give the game something different.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, that's what I'm thinking as well,<br /> the paragraph about the sabbat in the corebook feels like it came straight out of VtR<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400566#post1400566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You sure they're not just returned to the cycle after digestion? Even if trapped, would such a soul feel it?</div> </div> </div> </div>very doubtful, wouldn't be as scary if that were the case,<br /> <br /> I remember reading somewhere that the soul of the victim would get shattered and assimiliated,<br /> the black veins were the remaining fragments of the soul,<br /> the more willpower the victom had, the more black veins you got<br /> <br /> I don't remember which book that was though (a 2nd ed book, I think)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T15:28:12-07:00","id":1400587,"title":"","content":"I recommedn THE SEVEN FIRES section of THE CHICAGO FOLIO as a possibility. Mind you, Justin may take it in an entirely different direction than the 7F.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T15:52:37-07:00","id":1400589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400551#post1400551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it is. Its not supposed to be good for you. Like Sith Philosophy the &quot;diablere is awesome&quot; is meant to be hollow. Its meant to be a lie. Its meant to justify a quick and dangerous path to power. The reason why every person on Golconda successfully leaves vampire society is because its a game you cannot win. Every move is just a different method of losing. Diablere's &quot;Loss&quot; condition is becoming someone's new body of a wight.<br /> <br /> Actually lets consider instead how many vampires become wights even without Diablere. How many vampires are expected to survive even a human life time much less bask in &quot;Immortality&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thing is, that came in revised, in 2e paths COULD hit a form of Golconda, no one was the super special one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T16:01:03-07:00","id":1400591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400586#post1400586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> very doubtful, wouldn't be as scary if that were the case,<br /> <br /> I remember reading somewhere that the soul of the victim would get shattered and assimiliated,<br /> the black veins were the remaining fragments of the soul,<br /> the more willpower the victom had, the more black veins you got<br /> <br /> I don't remember which book that was though (a 2nd ed book, I think)</div> </div> </div> </div>Murder is pretty scary. I'll at least acknowledge that Diablerie is a painful process. Murdering a specific class of people for fun and profit? Terrifying if you're a member of that specific, threatened class.<br /> To me, a nuanced sociological evil that occurs naturally is a lot more dreadful than &quot;You ate a guy and now eternal suffering&quot;. I also find that losing agency over a character is rather boring. And, y'know, if I nearly get possessed every time I diablerise, I'm not going to do it again. <br /> <br /> I have to wonder what use and what long term effects would there be in keeping multiple souls in one body? Also, one must wonder why the chilling aura and black marks of diablerie fade after a short amount of time.. Why is it that for the first two editions of VTM, Diablerie was simply considered murder and humanity rolls treated it as such? What use is a soul in a body? Vampires get their power from blood, not souls. <br /> <br /> That month of Erie presence? Maybe, just maybe, that's a time period where the soul is being processed. That could mean an agonizing torture, but probably isn't. It's probably sleeping. Souls don't exactly enter the next life with the memories of the past life intact. After that erie pressence is gone, and the stains are gone, do you really think the soul is still inside you? <br /> <br /> Like, It's fun to have ancient, high willpower vampires possess would-be diablerists, but for everyone else that's kinda lame. Everyone would super hate themselves for the time they murdered themselves. It'd be farcical. <br /> <br /> By most normal rulesets. Diablerie isn't even a quick shortcut to power; It's just the only way to get rid of bottlenecks. Diablerie doesn't give you more dots in potence (for more than a fleeting moment at least, but that's due to the consumption of elder blood) but reducing your generations through diablerie will allow you to get that potence 6 you've coveted. More blood per turn is great, but being able to bring your attributes up is generally not as good as having lots of discipline dots. Getting permanent lots of permanent disciplines is kinda stupid and way too generous in all official and unofficial .rules i've seen. It's not a shortcut to certain powers; it's the only way to certain powers. <br /> <br /> (also if God did all this stuff why?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T16:25:40-07:00","id":1400594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400591#post1400591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to wonder what use and what long term effects would there be in keeping multiple souls in one body? Also, one must wonder why the chilling aura and black marks of diablerie fade after a short amount of time.. Why is it that for the first two editions of VTM, Diablerie was simply considered murder and humanity rolls treated it as such? What use is a soul in a body? Vampires get their power from blood, not souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>it was also used to gain the victims memories and learn from their experience,<br /> Sascha Vykos, for example, used to diablerize scholars to gain knowledge,<br /> sabbat on the path of Caine even encouraged elders to diablerize youngsters to get a...modern perspective,<br /> <br /> diablerie was a crude, and kinda messy, method to achieve it<br /> a more refined method is Valeren or Chi'uh Mu (the kuei jin version), which allow you to extract a soul and...do whatever you want with it, including consuming it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (also if God did all this stuff why?) </div> </div> </div>that wasn't god, god only cursed caine,<br /> what happened after wasn't god's doing,<br /> the embrace was taught by demons,<br /> the blood bond by the crone,<br /> disciplines by lilith,<br /> and generation was a curse put by caine to prevent childer from rebelling against their elders (sabbat would go nuts if they ever learned that)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400587#post1400587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommedn THE SEVEN FIRES section of THE CHICAGO FOLIO as a possibility. Mind you, Justin may take it in an entirely different direction than the 7F.</div> </div> </div> </div>don't you find that ironic, that the Seven Fires have &quot;Seven&quot; in their name? :x<br /> it's like they're not even trying to be subtle<br /> <br /> &quot;No longer are they the Leatherface, Hydra, and Joker sect so much as the Ed Gein, ISIS, and John Wayne Gacy sect.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm gonna have a hard time enjoying the sect now...Ed Gain I can stomach (pun intended), but Gacy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T16:30:32-07:00","id":1400595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400594#post1400594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">don't you find that ironic, that the Seven Fires have &quot;Seven&quot; in their name? :x<br /> it's like they're not even trying to be subtle<br /> <br /> &quot;No longer are they the Leatherface, Hydra, and Joker sect so much as the Ed Gein, ISIS, and John Wayne Gacy sect.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm gonna have a hard time enjoying the sect now...Ed Gain I can stomach (pun intended), but Gacy...</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is the Seven Fires are NOTHING like the Seven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T16:40:26-07:00","id":1400596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400595#post1400595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with that is the Seven Fires are NOTHING like the Seven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take your word for it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T16:44:38-07:00","id":1400597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400596#post1400596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll take your word for it</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they're a cell-based terrorist organization making attempts to assassinate the Lasombra and disrupt Camarilla rule while living normal lives inside the Camarilla. They also are terrifying mortals to disrupt the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Pretty standard Sabbat infiltration tactics, except they don't answer to a heirarchy anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T18:02:03-07:00","id":1400604,"title":"","content":"Hopefully they'll use something like this for the Sabbat: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z5WJa4WcghanB-mSGqdqIymRB7vteu/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z...ymRB7vteu/view</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T19:00:28-07:00","id":1400610,"title":"","content":"My irresponsible and reckless speculation about the Sabbat is\u2026<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The classic Sabbat no longer exists. It has been altered and shattered beyond repair and recognition.</li> <li>There will be multiple small factions and cells calling that each believe themselves to be the inheritors, or survivors, of the \u201creal Sabbat.\u201d These groups will call themselves different things.</li> <li>Some of these survivors will be content with survival. Others will seek some ideology to justify themselves and their bloody appetites.</li> <li>Lucita will probably be involved with one of the more agnostic cells, or at least one with the fewest religious trappings.</li> <li>Sasha will probably be involved with one of the more pious cells, or at least one with more religious trappings.</li> <li>Mimes will be involved.</li> <li>Multiple cells will be controlled, directly or indirectly, by former Sabbat members now controlled by some elder they diablerized.</li> <li>A massive part of the jyhad is a dog chasing its tail, with the ancients setting the younger vampires after each other in bloody minded games. What the Sabbat left behind, and what those remain do, will simply be a part of this process.</li> <li>The fractured nature of the Sabbat remains means they might well be found anywhere, in any city, among any sect. Anyone you know may or may not be a former member of the Sabbat. Maybe they are acting the way they do, or saying what they say, because they used to be (and still are at heart) Sabbat.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T20:13:25-07:00","id":1400619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400594#post1400594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> don't you find that ironic, that the Seven Fires have &quot;Seven&quot; in their name? :x<br /> it's like they're not even trying to be subtle</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I don't know why he even keeps referencing them as 'here's what the Sabbat might look like.' They're one specific small group doing their own thing, and aren't reflective of OTHER things we've seen written about the Sabbat, such as the Lasombra's specifics on why they left. They are a bad example to point at and look and say 'see this is what the Sabbat will probably be!' because they're not, in the scheme of what we've already seen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T22:17:02-07:00","id":1400633,"title":"","content":"I expect it\u2019s correct that the remaining Sabbat will be quite a number of different things simultaneously, given the lack of centralization and the fact that isolated terrorist cells is the operative metaphor. And clandestine witch covens, which is an old metaphor that makes sense again for many of them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:55:39-07:00","id":1400652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400557#post1400557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Demiurge (the idea of a blatantly evil God) is from Kult, not Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It appeared first in DA:V iirc, and since it is taken from real historical religious movements (Gnostic churches prominent among them) it's not 'from Kult'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 07-03-2020, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T01:55:38-07:00","id":1400662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400557#post1400557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Demiurge (the idea of a blatantly evil God) is from Kult, not Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gnosticism is where Kult got that from and is 2000 years old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T02:25:35-07:00","id":1400664,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> I know. I know what Gnosticism is. I just meant the Demiurge was a thing in Kult, not in Vampire. I do think the portrayal of God in the WoD is more nuanced than just an evil Demiurge. In H:tR he\u2019s the patron of the Messengers. In V:tM he curses Caine out of an Old Testament sense of morality. It\u2019s only in D:tF that you really get an outright selfish or \u201cevil\u201d God.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:21:38-07:00","id":1400677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400619#post1400619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. I don't know why he even keeps referencing them as 'here's what the Sabbat might look like.' They're one specific small group doing their own thing, and aren't reflective of OTHER things we've seen written about the Sabbat, such as the Lasombra's specifics on why they left. They are a bad example to point at and look and say 'see this is what the Sabbat will probably be!' because they're not, in the scheme of what we've already seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, I'm convinced we all realize we don't have a full picture of the sabbat,<br /> he just presented the seven fires as a counter argument to our theory about sabbat being VII/BB,<br /> and I'm using the other descriptions of the sabbat as my argument that they are VII/BB,<br /> <br /> might be just the devs being undecisive and contradicting themselves, or the sabbat being many things at the same time,<br /> <br /> whatever the case, let's just stick to theorizing,<br /> since this is a speculation thread, and not &quot;this is what the sabbat is&quot; thread (like the last one), his theories are as valid as ours \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400664#post1400664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>afaik, God was always depicted as either evil or vain,<br /> canonically, God only likes &quot;nice&quot; vampires, but that doesn't make God less evil<br /> <br /> some cults see God as being the evil demiurge from gnostic myth (the Setites, Cathari, Celestial Chorus, Cainite Heresy etc)<br /> <br /> but canonically, God is Yahweh, and gnostics are wrong,<br /> well, not 100% wrong, because Garou and Mage Methaphysics do hint at a possibility that Gnostics might be right about some things","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:24:53-07:00","id":1400679,"title":"","content":"Ah, right, this is an interesting topic <br /> <br /> Christianity had Gnostics. One idea was that the god in the old testament was the evil demiurge (Destroying the tower of Babel, flooding the earth, incinerating like six cities because two of them seemed to be police states/rapists/gay depending on how you take that 'so we may know them' ) and that Jesus represents a higher god that can deliver people from earth. (alternatively maybe you could see jesus as a comforting lie sent by the demiurge...) The Demiurge is supposed to be a fairly low-teir god and occasionally things from higher or equal gods fall into reality; This could explain vampires, mages and possibly the imbued (I don't think this applies to werewolves; they don't really have a path up to god-levels with spirits controlling what powers they get, and they largely function to keep the status quo. The Imbued might also be in this category) <br /> <br /> Another thing; So like, A corperation hands out rainbow cups when it sells coffee for pride month and supports black lives matter: Do you think this is a benevolent altruistic act or do you think that corperation has realised how profitable looking progressive is? If god does something nice, is that because he's a nice guy or is that because he wants you to worship him and abandon your resentment towards him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:26:37-07:00","id":1400680,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think most Sabbat are Gnostics. Most are quite content to believe that the Hebrew God is real and a bastard. Their malthestic messiah is Caine rather than Lucifer, however. Their version of Heaven is also this reality.<br /> <br /> &quot;We defy the God who cursed Cain and reveal in his power in our Heaven, WHICH IS EARTH WHERE WE SHALL REIGN IMMORTAL!&quot;<br /> -Sabbat who is getting too into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:40:20-07:00","id":1400684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400680#post1400680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't think most Sabbat are Gnostics. Most are quite content to believe that the Hebrew God is real and a bastard. Their malthestic messiah is Caine rather than Lucifer, however. Their version of Heaven is also this reality.<br /> <br /> &quot;We defy the God who cursed Cain and reveal in his power in our Heaven, WHICH IS EARTH WHERE WE SHALL REIGN IMMORTAL!&quot;<br /> -Sabbat who is getting too into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, gnosticism was very much a Cainite Heresy thing, not so much a Sabbat thing .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:41:50-07:00","id":1400685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400679#post1400679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Demiurge is supposed to be a fairly low-teir god and occasionally things from higher or equal gods fall into reality; This could explain vampires, mages and possibly the imbued (I don't think this applies to werewolves; they don't really have a path up to god-levels with spirits controlling what powers they get, and they largely function to keep the status quo. The Imbued might also be in this category)</div> </div> </div> </div>well, gaia and the triat do hint at there being a celestial bureaucracy reigning over reality,<br /> the demiurge could be a low tier god from the hierarchy, or it could be an interpretation of the Wyrm or something...but eh, it's wild speculation from my part<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:55:35-07:00","id":1400688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400684#post1400684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, gnosticism was very much a Cainite Heresy thing, not so much a Sabbat thing .</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, many Sabbat are atheists and just kind of go along with the Caine stuff. Which is part of what makes them vulnerable to demons.<br /> <br /> They're smart enough to have an Inquisition, though. Unlike the Anarchs who would scoff at the idea of demons existing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400685#post1400685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> well, gaia and the triat do hint at there being a celestial bureaucracy reigning over reality,<br /> the demiurge could be a low tier god from the hierarchy, or it could be an interpretation of the Wyrm or something...but eh, it's wild speculation from my part</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Black Fury's Patriarch is considered Wyrm tainted [really developers?-Me], I think the Demiurge by nature would be best exemplified by the Weaver. The whole point of the Weaver is keeping the entirety of humanity locked away in stasis, ignorant, and unchanging.<br /> <br /> The Seers of the Throne embody what a Demiurge-based group would be like over in Mage:Awakening","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-03-2020, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T04:48:36-07:00","id":1400696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400688#post1400688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Seers of the Throne embody what a Demiurge-based group would be like over in Mage:Awakening</div> </div> </div> </div>Most specifically, the Ministry of Paternoster. Woah, I love that group and I would love to have them in a Mage: the Ascension chronicle, if I thought I would be able to translate them correctly...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T05:18:17-07:00","id":1400702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400696#post1400696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most specifically, the Ministry of Paternoster. Woah, I love that group and I would love to have them in a Mage: the Ascension chronicle, if I thought I would be able to translate them correctly...</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually combined Chronicles of Darkness and World of Darkness during the 10 year break.<br /> <br /> The SEERS OF THE THRONE are the result of the Technocratic Union being divided by the Avatar Storm. They made contact with the Exarchs, who are either the Oracles ascended from the Technocracy or they are Axions of the Weaver that exist solely for the purpose of creating a world without magic. The Seers of the Throne are a bit (a VERY bit) tiny more sympathetic in that they think a world where only they have sorcery and Mass Ascension is a lie is still &quot;close enough&quot; to their utopia. They also receive guarantees of safety, security, and wealth for their families as well as themselves. They're then given the Big GunsTM to go resume the Ascension War. The Seers promptly absorb the Knights Templars and several corrupt members of the Tradition to start using religion to serve their new masters aims too.<br /> <br /> THE REST of the Union is horrified by what they perceive as a betrayal just slightly less egregious than allying with the Nephandi and becoming traitors to the human race. They thus end up allying with the Traditions didn't join the seers. Even then, they're both a fraction of their former power.<br /> <br /> I did the same for Vampire, Changeling, and Werewolf in terms of combining them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T05:27:44-07:00","id":1400704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400664#post1400664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> I know. I know what Gnosticism is. I just meant the Demiurge was a thing in Kult, not in Vampire. I do think the portrayal of God in the WoD is more nuanced than just an evil Demiurge. In H:tR he\u2019s the patron of the Messengers. In V:tM he curses Caine out of an Old Testament sense of morality. It\u2019s only in D:tF that you really get an outright selfish or \u201cevil\u201d God.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correction: In DtF you get how most demons see God. Doesn't mean their perception (or bias) is correct. The same is true about how Lilith sees God in Revelations of the Dark Mother and so on. The Cainite Heresy system of belief was (is since V5 resurrected them) gnostic. Doesn't mean they were/are right, not anymore than setites believing their progenitor stands for freedom and some Sabbat believing they are the scions of Caine called to purge the Earth from the Antediluvians and their servants...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T05:35:08-07:00","id":1400707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400704#post1400704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correction: In DtF you get how most demons see God. Doesn't mean their perception (or bias) is correct. The same is true about how Lilith sees God in Revelations of the Dark Mother and so on. The Cainite Heresy system of belief was (is since V5 resurrected them) gnostic. Doesn't mean they were/are right, not anymore than setites believing their progenitor stands for freedom and some Sabbat believing they are the scions of Caine called to purge the Earth from the Antediluvians and their servants...</div> </div> </div> </div>They even twisted that in D:TF as they pointed out that God may have actually been saving the universe from the demons having unraveled some of its foundational elements by giving humans magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T05:51:39-07:00","id":1400709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400707#post1400707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They even twisted that in D:TF as they pointed out that God may have actually been saving the universe from the demons having unraveled some of its foundational elements by giving humans magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's highly debatable. In Demon the Fallen some demons really hate humanity because they learnt how humanity's growth would make it capable of dominating and enslaving demons and angels alike. Adam being given the power to name things by God meant he got power over them as well, the original humans in D:tF are supposed to have greater unchecked magical potential than the current ones simply because there was no paradox or backlash back then.<br /> <br /> So God not wanting humans to have magic is one interpretation of what happened but to me it feels like justification from some demons for their war not something that happened &quot;for sure&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T05:57:19-07:00","id":1400711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400709#post1400709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's highly debatable. In Demon the Fallen some demons really hate humanity because they learnt how humanity's growth would make it capable of dominating and enslaving demons and angels alike. Adam being given the power to name things by God meant he got power over them as well, the original humans in D:tF are supposed to have greater unchecked magical potential than the current ones simply because there was no paradox or backlash back then.<br /> <br /> So God not wanting humans to have magic is one interpretation of what happened but to me it feels like justification from some demons for their war not something that happened &quot;for sure&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the trilogy they had this conversation:<br /> <br /> &quot;God struck the world and destroyed all our works.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you sure he did?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What if he was catching the world as it fell.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T06:00:18-07:00","id":1400712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400688#post1400688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell, many Sabbat are atheists and just kind of go along with the Caine stuff. Which is part of what makes them vulnerable to demons.<br /> <br /> They're smart enough to have an Inquisition, though. Unlike the Anarchs who would scoff at the idea of demons existing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While the Black Fury's Patriarch is considered Wyrm tainted [really developers?-Me], I think the Demiurge by nature would be best exemplified by the Weaver. The whole point of the Weaver is keeping the entirety of humanity locked away in stasis, ignorant, and unchanging.<br /> <br /> The Seers of the Throne embody what a Demiurge-based group would be like over in Mage:Awakening</div> </div> </div> </div>Demiurge as a crazed Weaver Incarna or maybe Celestine? That could be fun. And yea all the sects need an inquisition,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T06:03:39-07:00","id":1400714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400711#post1400711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the trilogy they had this conversation:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;God struck the world and destroyed all our works.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Are you sure he did?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;What if he was catching the world as it fell.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is an example of why I have a love/hate thing going on with DtF, it tells really good stories sometimes, while tying the entire WoD to a Christianised mythos, and by implication of not intention, declaring all other faiths and myths false","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T06:07:35-07:00","id":1400715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400714#post1400714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is an example of why I have a love/hate thing going on with DtF, it tells really good stories sometimes, while tying the entire WoD to a Christianised mythos, and by implication of not intention, declaring all other faiths and myths false</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to call you out on this but I sense there's a very specific bias against Abrahamic religious specifically because it completely ignores that there's ample evidence of the truth of other faiths that are are treated as literally true.<br /> <br /> Or, in other words, &quot;So, how much do you hate Werewolf: The Apocalypse and Wraith: The Oblivion for disproving Christianity?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T06:24:33-07:00","id":1400717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400715#post1400715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to call you out on this but I sense there's a very specific bias against Abrahamic religious specifically because it completely ignores that there's ample evidence of the truth of other faiths that are are treated as literally true.<br /> <br /> Or, in other words, &amp;quot;So, how much do you hate Werewolf: The Apocalypse and Wraith: The Oblivion for disproving Christianity?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much, but if they had proven Zoroastrianism, or the Vedic Pantheon or (insert other real world faith here) I would have been a lot less happy, fantasy faiths I have no problems with, dead faiths get a pass as well, but embracing an active religion has a pile of problems (both with accidently making a mess of it, and with the 'everyone else is wrong' problem, it's why I enjoy Tolkien but not C S Lewis, to give another example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T07:14:09-07:00","id":1400730,"title":"","content":"I think DtF cosmology being more straightforward was a point in its favour,<br /> it was a nice change from the overly ambiguous and confusing cosmologies from other lines,<br /> <br /> not saying that ambiguity is a bad thing,<br /> but at times, it can become really exhausting,<br /> and some players feel that since everything is so ambiguous, better just play the atheist that doesn't give two shits about who is the god of what<br /> <br /> I suspect that was one reason (not the only one, I know) Roads were more popular than paths<br /> <br /> sometimes, you just need a break from all the mind gymnatics,<br /> DtF told you what you were, where you came from, what others like you were fighting against and why,<br /> now, do whatever you want with that info...BAM! simple and effective<br /> <br /> again, I'm not saying this is the right way to do things,<br /> I just happen to like DtF's design as much as I liked the other ones","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T07:48:51-07:00","id":1400733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400702#post1400702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually combined Chronicles of Darkness and World of Darkness during the 10 year break.<br /> <br /> The SEERS OF THE THRONE are the result of the Technocratic Union being divided by the Avatar Storm. They made contact with the Exarchs, who are either the Oracles ascended from the Technocracy or they are Axions of the Weaver that exist solely for the purpose of creating a world without magic. The Seers of the Throne are a bit (a VERY bit) tiny more sympathetic in that they think a world where only they have sorcery and Mass Ascension is a lie is still &amp;quot;close enough&amp;quot; to their utopia. They also receive guarantees of safety, security, and wealth for their families as well as themselves. They're then given the Big GunsTM to go resume the Ascension War. The Seers promptly absorb the Knights Templars and several corrupt members of the Tradition to start using religion to serve their new masters aims too.<br /> <br /> THE REST of the Union is horrified by what they perceive as a betrayal just slightly less egregious than allying with the Nephandi and becoming traitors to the human race. They thus end up allying with the Traditions didn't join the seers. Even then, they're both a fraction of their former power.<br /> <br /> I did the same for Vampire, Changeling, and Werewolf in terms of combining them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love your Mage combo!<br /> <br /> I want to ask a question about the Patriarch. Should I ask it here or create a new thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T08:42:59-07:00","id":1400746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400714#post1400714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is an example of why I have a love/hate thing going on with DtF, it tells really good stories sometimes, while tying the entire WoD to a Christianised mythos, and by implication of not intention, declaring all other faiths and myths false</div> </div> </div> </div>D:tF also includes eastern faiths as antagonistic to the Earthbound. If any faiths have been skrewed over by D:tF is the polytheistic ones, the ancient ones in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T09:15:26-07:00","id":1400758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400733#post1400733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love your Mage combo!<br /> <br /> I want to ask a question about the Patriarch. Should I ask it here or create a new thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, go ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T09:52:47-07:00","id":1400765,"title":"","content":"Back on Sabbat Speculation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a 'mind the gap' chronicle detailing the changes to the Sabbat between V20 and V5.<br /> <br /> Civil war, beckoning, antidiluvian hunting etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T10:58:34-07:00","id":1400780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400765#post1400765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on Sabbat Speculation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a 'mind the gap' chronicle detailing the changes to the Sabbat between V20 and V5.<br /> <br /> Civil war, beckoning, antidiluvian hunting etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting take would be to handle it like Technocracy V20, though I don't think they'd do it. We wouldn't necessarily begin with the Sabbat as they were in V5 at the start but explain how things went from Revised to Beckett's Jyhad Diarty to the Gehenna War to what the current status quo would be.<br /> <br /> One thing I do think is that Justin Achilli is FAR more comfortable with the level of darkness and casual brutality of &quot;villain protagonists&quot; than some of the previous developers were.<br /> <br /> Ergo, Sabbat player characters will be fine for him the same way Giovanni were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:22:48-07:00","id":1400789,"title":"","content":"How is the Patriarch related to the Judeo-Christian God YHVH of Vampire, Hunter and Demon? Are they allies? Rivals? The same being?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":".  Meant to capitalize God 07-03-2020, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:34:50-07:00","id":1400791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400789#post1400789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the Patriarch related to the Judeo-Christian God YHVH of Vampire, Hunter and Demon? Are they allies? Rivals? The same being?<br /> <br /> Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Black Furies believe the Patriarch is the Christian God and the source of humanity getting all their icky monotheism in what is obviously a polytheistic world. They would believe the Demons to be Wyrm-tainted and obviously insane spirits.<br /> <br /> The Demons claim that the Spirit World was created by them as a system to manage and maintain reality, only to go off the rails when it became sentient.<br /> <br /> In effect, the Demons claim that GAIA and the Triat is the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Notable fact: God is missing in the World of Darkness and Heaven is empty. One possible interpretation for this is that he's broken himself up among humans and that's where avatars came from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:36:56-07:00","id":1400793,"title":"","content":"Oh wow...<br /> <br /> Thank you \ud83d\ude0a. That really inspires me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T14:48:45-07:00","id":1400824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400791#post1400791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notable fact: God is missing in the World of Darkness and Heaven is empty. One possible interpretation for this is that he's broken himself up among humans and that's where avatars came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always enjoyed the (not-entirely-serious) theory that G#d got tired of the World of Darkness universe, and went off to create the Chronicles of Darkness universe instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T14:51:51-07:00","id":1400825,"title":"","content":"It's definitely a fun idea, plus if you are so inclined there's enough Easter eggs in CoD (particularly 1e) to imagine how things might transmute from the WoD to CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T15:22:30-07:00","id":1400832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400824#post1400824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always enjoyed the (not-entirely-serious) theory that G#d got tired of the World of Darkness universe, and went off to create the Chronicles of Darkness universe instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unconquered Sun is off to the Games of Divinity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T17:06:54-07:00","id":1400853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400780#post1400780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An interesting take would be to handle it like Technocracy V20, though I don't think they'd do it. We wouldn't necessarily begin with the Sabbat as they were in V5 at the start but explain how things went from Revised to Beckett's Jyhad Diarty to the Gehenna War to what the current status quo would be.<br /> <br /> One thing I do think is that Justin Achilli is FAR more comfortable with the level of darkness and casual brutality of &quot;villain protagonists&quot; than some of the previous developers were.<br /> <br /> Ergo, Sabbat player characters will be fine for him the same way Giovanni were.</div> </div> </div> </div>/Sigh<br /> <br /> I must be the only person in the world who actually liked the Giovanni as they were. I have zero enthusiasm to get into the Cappadocians MKII. Yeah, I know it's said the Giovanni are still the ones most in leadership positions... after their Elders got destroyed, they had the Harbingers move in (who are infinitely stronger than them), the entire Clan got renamed (not a fan of the name either; at least make it 'scions of Hecata' or something), their discipline spread reverted back to the Cappadocian model... right. I'm not buying it.<br /> <br /> As for the Sabbat. I fully expect them to have become way, way meaner. After their little sabbatical (hah) where they had ample time to get rid of posers, weaklings, anyone not sufficiently fanatical. They need to be to have an identity outside the Anarchs. Heck, it's possible the Sabbat will shed some outliers like the Old Clan or the Oradea League\u2014maybe to the Camarilla, if they feel like the last Anarch experiment was too humiliating a failure and the Usurpers are weak enough to push out from inside with time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T17:11:30-07:00","id":1400854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400853#post1400853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> /Sigh<br /> <br /> I must be the only person in the world who actually liked the Giovanni as they were. I have zero enthusiasm to get into the Cappadocians MKII. Yeah, I know it's said the Giovanni are still the ones most in leadership positions... after their Elders got destroyed, they had the Harbingers move in (who are infinitely stronger than them), the entire Clan got renamed (not a fan of the name either; at least make it 'scions of Hecata' or something), their discipline spread reverted back to the Cappadocian model... right. I'm not buying it.<br /> <br /> As for the Sabbat. I fully expect them to have become way, way meaner. After their little sabbatical (hah) where they had ample time to get rid of posers, weaklings, anyone not sufficiently fanatical. They need to be to have an identity outside the Anarchs. Heck, it's possible the Sabbat will shed some outliers like the Old Clan or the Oradea League\u2014maybe to the Camarilla, if they feel like the last Anarch experiment was too humiliating a failure and the Usurpers are weak enough to push out from inside with time.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation is the fact Harbingers have no interest in running the Giovanni's empire. It's made of businesses, smuggling, human trafficking, and cannibalism.<br /> <br /> The Harbingers have no interest in all of that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T17:39:19-07:00","id":1400862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400854#post1400854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My interpretation is the fact Harbingers have no interest in running the Giovanni's empire. It's made of businesses, smuggling, human trafficking, and cannibalism.<br /> <br /> The Harbingers have no interest in all of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still feels like a missed opportunity to have a Giovanni faction join the Camarilla. The Promise of 1528 having 500-year time limit, plus increasing hostilities from the Harbingers was a great setup for it, and a really interesting idea in general.<br /> <br /> Also, how will the Sabbat react to the Harbingers dropping out? They were never a great power, but they had influence. They'd made a splash. And the Sword of Caine doesn't strike me as just accepting resignations. Heck, maybe the Harbingers are worried the allies they'd used and thrown away will come back to collect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T19:15:48-07:00","id":1400878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400862#post1400862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still feels like a missed opportunity to have a Giovanni faction join the Camarilla. The Promise of 1528 having 500-year time limit, plus increasing hostilities from the Harbingers was a great setup for it, and a really interesting idea in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Promise of 1528 is about making sure they DON'T join the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The terms of the Promise are effectively:<br /> <br /> * The Camarilla will let the Giovanni commit genocide on the Cappadocians<br /> * The Giovanni will stay out of the Camarilla's way and not aid the Sabbat or Anarchs.<br /> <br /> So you can see why the Harbingers aren't fond of the Cammies, especially when the Cappadocians asked to join the Camarilla for protection only to have them cut this deal instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how will the Sabbat react to the Harbingers dropping out? They were never a great power, but they had influence. They'd made a splash. And the Sword of Caine doesn't strike me as just accepting resignations. Heck, maybe the Harbingers are worried the allies they'd used and thrown away will come back to collect... </div> </div> </div>Funny, I'm more concerned about how the TRUE HAND would feel about the Harbingers not only dropping out but taking their founders with them. The Nagaraja were as important to the True Hand as the Lasombra were to the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T20:01:45-07:00","id":1400884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400878#post1400878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the Promise of 1528 is about making sure they DON'T join the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The terms of the Promise are effectively:<br /> <br /> * The Camarilla will let the Giovanni commit genocide on the Cappadocians<br /> * The Giovanni will stay out of the Camarilla's way and not aid the Sabbat or Anarchs.<br /> <br /> So you can see why the Harbingers aren't fond of the Cammies, especially when the Cappadocians asked to join the Camarilla for protection only to have them cut this deal instead.<br /> <br /> Funny, I'm more concerned about how the TRUE HAND would feel about the Harbingers not only dropping out but taking their founders with them. The Nagaraja were as important to the True Hand as the Lasombra were to the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. I'm just saying, Augustus going poof, the Sabbat attacking more and more openly because of those weird, ancient premascines, and then finding out the contract forbidding you from joining the Camarilla is expiring soon, isn't all of that a good reason to start negotiating for formal membership? Sounds more logical to me than expecting the Harbingers to just suddenly stop going after you. Maybe only part of the family. In fact, that could still happen if enough Giovanni are unhappy and wish to leave their new bloodcult.<br /> <br /> The True Hand is a whole 'nother can of worms, true. I would not be totally surprised if the Sabbat managed to excise most of their influence by now. Maybe it's unfair, but the Tal'mahe'Ra seemed really... inept, at times. Very powerful inidividually, but as an organisation, not so much. Too caught up in their own self-importance to see the forest for the trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T20:26:01-07:00","id":1400889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400878#post1400878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, I'm more concerned about how the TRUE HAND would feel about the Harbingers not only dropping out but taking their founders with them. The Nagaraja were as important to the True Hand as the Lasombra were to the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the Week of Nightmares happened in V5 canon, I figure Enoch got blown up pretty good too. Hence the Nagaraja looking for protection elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T01:35:37-07:00","id":1400915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread#post1400491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Justin Achilli having taken over as Creator Director</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, as a V5 critic, this is the thing that has made me the most hopeful for seeing V5 salvaged (for me) narratively thus far. I've liked a lot of what he's done, disagreed or hated some, but my general opinion was positive. I'm down for his possible interpretation of the Sabbat in V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T01:44:48-07:00","id":1400918,"title":"","content":"See, with the Giovanni eating the capadocians, I took it as a metaphore for how a well organized agressive organization will crush small Mum'n dad businesses. It was a mirror image of what the Tremere did with the Salubri. It thus doesn't make a lot of sense that the surviving capadocians who are all ancient helped in a revolution to destroy that organization. I mean, yeah, maybe there's some anti-monopoly metaphor there, but we live in an age where everyone's getting more monopolistic so it completely goes against the zeitgeist. <br /> <br /> I think the Gehena war is a rediculous farce. Best reasoning available: it's an elder ploy to kill off the sabbat neonates so that the sabbat elders can join the nuCamarilla without contention. The Sabbat will come back with a reckoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T06:29:50-07:00","id":1400949,"title":"","content":"Do you expect more Sabbat crossing over to the Cam in the process, MWIS?<br /> <br /> I'm all for the Camarilla getting more options. It struck me as silly how the Sabbat had choice for everything under the moon while the supposedly bigger sect either shrunk, or the options they did have that were unique to them (i.e. Gargoyles) were a complete non-factor and close to actively discouraged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:10:16-07:00","id":1400971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400918#post1400918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, with the Giovanni eating the capadocians, I took it as a metaphore for how a well organized agressive organization will crush small Mum'n dad businesses. It was a mirror image of what the Tremere did with the Salubri.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with this theory is that capitalism didn't really come into being until the seventeenth century, and the concept of a well-run corporation crushing mom-and-pop businesses wasn't established until well after the 1400s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:22:37-07:00","id":1400972,"title":"","content":"The fact that the Camarilla are now openly, rather than secretly, religious indicates to me that they made some consesions with some Sabbat elders who were going to prop up the organization when the Camarilla let a lot of it's members go to the anarchs and the Sabbat sent their young to the middle east. (The added religious appeal unfortunately makes them look like Republicans, but I don't know if that's happenstance or the desired result)<br /> <br /> There are a lot of cities with sensible Sabbat left behind (with the firebrands purged) and the Sabbat are needed their to keep their tendrils into mortal society and ensure a seemless transition (The Sabbat completely leaving these cities, and the Camarilla completely moving in, would be an absolute logistical disaster) . All Sabbat with good connections are going to be canidates for the Camarilla transition (Or a purge) whilst the loose lot too involved in the circlejerk to have any serious mortal holdings are of absolutely no use to the NuCamarilla.<br /> <br /> Hey, It could be that <i>absolutely nobody is heading towards the middle east</i> and really the guys arranging transport are just mass killing sabbat in their sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Camarilla getting new options works with how they're now the religious group. But I never thought it strange that the cam had so few clans in it as those clans clearly have the most reproductive potential (In nature, generalists do better than specialists, and clan specific disciplines are the result of specialists)<br /> <br /> I feel they'll make a lot of treaties, especially concering the two T's; The many many elders in the Camarilla don't like Vicissitude (which might be the Tremere's doing), and many elders don' t want it to spread into their cities. Conversely, the Tremere aren't to enter certain cities because they'd certainly fight with the former Sabbat (perhaps this is why the Tremere so masterfully staged Vienna; So they can enter these cities under the guise of house Carna)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:27:57-07:00","id":1400973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400971#post1400971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue with this theory is that capitalism didn't really come into being until the seventeenth century, and the concept of a well-run corporation crushing mom-and-pop businesses wasn't established until well after the 1400s.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Modern capitalism, yeah, Mercantillism became a thing in the 15th century, the very century that our corpse-fucking family rose up. It's not a coincidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:32:56-07:00","id":1400976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400971#post1400971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue with this theory is that capitalism didn't really come into being until the seventeenth century, and the concept of a well-run corporation crushing mom-and-pop businesses wasn't established until well after the 1400s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's reaching a bit there but it would a Doylist not Watsonian view anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:38:32-07:00","id":1400977,"title":"","content":"<b>How I would do the Gehenna War's Aftermath</b><br /> <br /> My take on the Gehenna Crusades and this is just speculation is that they are going to emerge as something that's actually analogous to the real-life Crusades. The Sabbat will return from the Middle East with a bunch of ancient tomes, scrolls, clay tablets, and stone writings that will go a long way to increasing their knowledge of ancient Kindred history as well as the power of their mystical factions. A bunch of barbarians entered the Middle East, what will emerge is a much more educated and intelligent group (at the cost of much bloodshed).<br /> <br /> They will also have many vampires who will have emerged changed from the ancient blood they've drank. There will be a couple of Mithras-types among them but, by and large, it will simply be that the Sabbat was victorious NOT over sleeping Methuesalshs but having exterminated hundreds of <b>Camarilla elders</b> who were Beckoned.<br /> <br /> The Antediluvians will have drank their bloody fill during this time and have altered the memories of the Sabbat the same way the Tzimisce and Lasombra Elders did. They will remember being the ones to have killed so many Cammies and have achieved greater victories over the Ivory Tower than they have in their entire history since the First Anarch Revolt. Whether it is a lie or not doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> The New Sabbat will emerge as a tighter more occult-based organization with almost none of its previous Anarch roots but much more akin to the True Hand or the Children of Zillah. Alien paths and ritual will almost completely dominate the sect with very little of the FREEEDDDDOM stuff that is now the province of the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> They will claim to have defeated the Antediluvians and will be secretly their foremost pawns.<br /> <br /> I also think that the Sabbat will have destroyed Alamut and claimed numerous domains in the Middle East with conflict in Jerusalem, Syria, and other notable places. They won't regain all of their cities but they will re-establish themselves in many places with Miami, Rio, Tripoli, Venezuela, and other places as good bases for their activities. They will be more interested in evangelizing than before with agents spread throughout the cities, designed to take them over from within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-04-2020, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:41:19-07:00","id":1400978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400862#post1400862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how will the Sabbat react to the Harbingers dropping out? They were never a great power, but they had influence. They'd made a splash. And the Sword of Caine doesn't strike me as just accepting resignations. Heck, maybe the Harbingers are worried the allies they'd used and thrown away will come back to collect...</div> </div> </div> </div>no, I doubt the sabbat would chase after them for revenge,<br /> the sabbat owed them more than they owed the sabbat,<br /> and one of the leaders of the sect (the lasombra) just packed up and left, selling out and murdering sect elders and neonates alike on their way out,<br /> <br /> if anything, it's the sabbat that betrayed the harbingers and not the other way around<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:44:12-07:00","id":1400980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400978#post1400978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no, I doubt the sabbat would chase after them for revenge,<br /> the sabbat owed them more than they owed the sabbat,<br /> and one of the leaders of the sect (the lasombra) just packed up and left, selling out and murdering sect elders and neonates alike on their way out,<br /> <br /> if anything, it's the sabbat that betrayed the harbingers and not the other way around</div> </div> </div> </div>It's questionable if the Harbingers will even say they've dropped out.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh no, we went and killed an Antedilivuan. We're totes in with you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T13:25:46-07:00","id":1400992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400976#post1400976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think he's reaching a bit there but it would a Doylist not Watsonian view anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was indeed using some artistic liscence, but indeed, both the well organized Tremere and Giovanni eating away at clans of relatively nice vampires and taking their place is a powerful fable for how vampires work. Both new clans acted like a tightly run business, both victim clans were adverse to politicking, spent a lot of time navel gazing, and largely got as far as they did because they weren't a threat to anyone . Mediocre non-threats who seem nice lose to the ambitious. Also Fortitude+Auspex isn't the defensive combination you'd think it'd be. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400977#post1400977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How I would do the Gehenna War's Aftermath</b><br /> <br /> My take on the Gehenna Crusades and this is just speculation is that they are going to emerge as something that's actually analogous to the real-life Crusades. The Sabbat will return from the Middle East with a bunch of ancient tomes, scrolls, clay tablets, and stone writings that will go a long way to increasing their knowledge of ancient Kindred history as well as the power of their mystical factions. A bunch of barbarians entered the Middle East, what will emerge is a much more educated and intelligent group (at the cost of much bloodshed).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they'll find... Nothing. Some crusades were better than others (and even the 'successful' crusades were full of Gaffs). Best case scenario they destroy some Infernalists, Worst case scenario they all become infernalists. Anything 'good' isn't written down and preserved for that long, and the Sabbat are more likely to destroy a relic than learn from it. <br /> <br /> Also, we no-longer live in a world where europeans are in a dark age and the middle east has preserved and continued all european knowledge. Europeans live in the information age. Now, yeah, I guess you could point out that most of the Sabbat are from the Americas, and In a lot of ways you could point to the USA as a regression, but most Sabbat aren't from the USA, they're from elsewhere in the Americas. <br /> <br /> Simply put, the context for 'recovering knowledge' isn't there, both from &quot;A Doylist and Watsonian view&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They will claim to have defeated the Antediluvians and will be secretly their foremost pawns. </div> </div> </div>To what end? Aren't the antideluvians trying to kill eachother and thus the Sabbat should be having a good time attacking Antis even if they're pawns of other Antis? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T13:41:49-07:00","id":1400994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400992#post1400992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they'll find... Nothing. Some crusades were better than others (and even the 'successful' crusades were full of Gaffs). Best case scenario they destroy some Infernalists, Worst case scenario they all become infernalists. Anything 'good' isn't written down and preserved for that long, and the Sabbat are more likely to destroy a relic than learn from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always liked the intellectual side of the Sabbat. Part of the fun of playing the Path of Caine Elder Tet-Anubis was the idea he was Belloq and an archaeologist while he had to deal with dumbass shovelheads breaking things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, we no-longer live in a world where europeans are in a dark age and the middle east has preserved and continued all european knowledge. Europeans live in the information age. Now, yeah, I guess you could point out that most of the Sabbat are from the Americas, and In a lot of ways you could point to the USA as a regression, but most Sabbat aren't from the USA, they're from elsewhere in the Americas. </div> </div> </div>None of said information is on the internet because Kindred like Mithras aren't idiots who write their ancient history down on Facebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simply put, the context for 'recovering knowledge' isn't there, both from &quot;A Doylist and Watsonian view&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how given they're awakening dozens of ancients and facing down hundreds of Methuselahs Beckoned to fight them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To what end? Aren't the antideluvians trying to kill eachother and thus the Sabbat should be having a good time attacking Antis even if they're pawns of other Antis? </div> </div> </div>In a few Gehenna ceremonies, the Antediluvians were all friends. The game is how they amuse themselves. Yes, they try and kill each other to rule alone but they're also each other's only companions.<br /> <br /> Just like other Elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T20:19:58-07:00","id":1401044,"title":"","content":"I've played around lately with the headcanon that the second generation doesn't exist and never did. The First Vampire, whoever it was, sired the Antediluvians to explore different aspects of undeath. Maybe [Caine] is tired of existence and wants an out. That's why so many of them are determined to transcend in some fashion or other. It's what they were created to do. Not unlike what the Eldest ended up doing with its childer.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat has traditionally been the Camarilla's nemesis, but that was before the Anarchs had any bite. They might become even greater enemies towards them now. Especially with the Ministry officially having joined. That is, if the Sword of Caine still believes to be fighting the Founders.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T04:14:13-07:00","id":1401088,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in what the Black Hand does. Are they the core of the Crusade? Is the Sabbat that goes to the Middle East being rendered down into being a more professional force like the Black Hand? Or has the Black Hand been broken due to a combination of the Inquisition and the main body of the Sabbat finding out little pieces of the True Hand? Or another option would be that the Black hand wants nothing to do with the Crusade and they're what gets left behind.<br /> <br /> A winnowing of the Sabbat makes sense given what's been presented so far. Low ranking members either got their stuff together (physically if not mentally) in the Middle East, died in the Middle East or went to the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> I think Paths get left out still. There is a price to pay for actions and no matter what you tell yourself about your morals you can't get away completely from what made you a human.<br /> <br /> From a less in game perspective one of the pressures keeping the Anarchs marginalised in previous editions was that to young player characters the Sabbat offered more fun and the same sticking it to the man ethos. I think you need to marginalise the Sabbat to promote the Anarchs. And promoting the Anarchs allows for much more interesting inter-sect politicking, both globally and within domains. I mean how much more interesting a default is it that there are two sects visible within a city that doesn't mean death when they interact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26282-lacheur","name":"Lacheur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T05:56:00-07:00","id":1401094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lacheur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401088#post1401088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a less in game perspective one of the pressures keeping the Anarchs marginalised in previous editions was that to young player characters the Sabbat offered more fun and the same sticking it to the man ethos. I think you need to marginalise the Sabbat to promote the Anarchs. And promoting the Anarchs allows for much more interesting inter-sect politicking, both globally and within domains. I mean how much more interesting a default is it that there are two sects visible within a city that doesn't mean death when they interact?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Yes, you are correct about the Sabbat marginalizing the Anarchs because both Sects were opposed to the Camarilla but the Sabbat being the more openly violent ended turning the ANarchs into a subsect of the Camarilla, the &quot;loyal opposition&quot; so to speak.<br /> <br /> No, the Sabbat had nothing to do with the concept of &quot;sticking it to the man&quot;, because at the end of the day packs answered to bishop, archbishops and cardinals, and basically all of those were elders and shady political figures, much like their counterparts in the Camarilla were.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T07:29:27-07:00","id":1401111,"title":"","content":"I don't like comparing the sabbat to the anarchs,<br /> since the sabbat, like the Camarilla, have their own Anarchs (called the Loyalists) who are just Anarchs with Vinculum<br /> <br /> the sabbat didn't offer more fun,<br /> they had worse clan weaknesses (unless you were lasombra) and weaker chargen (since sabbat had no points in backgrounds),<br /> and taking on a path required spending points on willpower and lose up to two points in virtues (depending on path)<br /> <br /> what the sabbat did offer, was a different way to play the horror,<br /> <br /> in the camarilla, age meant everything, elders hold all the privileges and the traditions protect them,<br /> your relationship to them will dictate your unlife, with the Anarchs as a possible escape<br /> <br /> in the sabbat, you are weak in a sect where power means everything,<br /> you can go loyalist (anarch), even challenge elders if you wish, but you have a bigger chance of just ending up dead,<br /> you can suck up to elders, but other packs will murder you for it,<br /> you can serve the sect as a crusader or whatever, but the price of failiure is become a tzimisce's torture toy,<br /> you can invest in human ressources and have local noddists murder your herd and your mortal contacts and hang you upside down for all the sabbat to mock you,<br /> <br /> the sabbat doesn't eclipse the anarchs, they just have their own flavour,<br /> and, in editions where the horror played a big part (revised edition being the main offender), the sabbat just had more to offer than the Anarchs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 07-05-2020, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T07:40:11-07:00","id":1401116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401111#post1401111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the sabbat doesn't eclipse the anarchs, they just have their own flavour,<br /> and, in editions where the horror played a big part (revised edition being the main offender), the sabbat just had more to offer than the Anarchs</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Sabbat has always been more splatter than horror.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T08:37:12-07:00","id":1401126,"title":"","content":"Kludge is an ill-assorted collection of parts assembled to fulfill a particular purpose. That describes the contents of most RPGs settings that have gone on for more than a few years. Bits of things get added onto and stick around just because.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat appeared in 1<sup>st</sup> edition VtM as a metaphoric fire to the skillet of the Camarilla. They were the monsters lurking in the dark, just part the edges of Camarilla power. If the characters didn\u2019t like dealing with the Camarilla \u2013 too bad. You can\u2019t leave, because the Sabbat will get you.<br /> <br /> The expansion of the game line meant they had to be explored at some point, which meant the Sabbat lost some of its mystique. They stopped being an unknown terror and became a bizarre blood cult.<br /> <br /> Yes, they were more splatter than horror. That wasn\u2019t so much by design as by accident.<br /> <br /> Whatever the Sabbat become can move deeper into actual horror territory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T08:37:39-07:00","id":1401127,"title":"","content":"Do you think that'll stay? It would give the Sabbat a niche, if they stay with gore-filled splatter over the political games and slow grinding away of humanity of the Camarilla or the Lost Boys rage against the machine of the Anarchs. On the other hand, it may make the sect look and feel... juvenile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T09:21:15-07:00","id":1401133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401127#post1401127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that'll stay? It would give the Sabbat a niche, if they stay with gore-filled splatter over the political games and slow grinding away of humanity of the Camarilla or the Lost Boys rage against the machine of the Anarchs. On the other hand, it may make the sect look and feel... juvenile.</div> </div> </div> </div>note that camarilla and their political games are juvenile as well,<br /> there's nothing mature about what they're doing, it's glorified high school drama<br /> <br /> the objective here isn't to make the sabbat look less childish, childish is what vampires in general are<br /> <br /> and, while I'm not against the sabbat being all about splatter, the whole thing just doesn't make sense in universe<br /> <br /> the 2e sabbat being all gorry about everything was fun and all,<br /> but it required alot of suspension of disbelief to accept that such a lifestyle was sustainable, or even possible","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T10:02:18-07:00","id":1401140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401127#post1401127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that'll stay? It would give the Sabbat a niche, if they stay with gore-filled splatter over the political games and slow grinding away of humanity of the Camarilla or the Lost Boys rage against the machine of the Anarchs. On the other hand, it may make the sect look and feel... juvenile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say that the Sabbat should be reinvisioned as a non-crappy version of the True Hand.<br /> <br /> Focus on the occult, mystical, demonic part of the sect.<br /> <br /> More Montreal ceremonies in the woods.<br /> <br /> Less slaughter-maim-destroyer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T01:53:28-07:00","id":1401300,"title":"","content":"I don't think they will find anything truly good in the middle east; any cainite trully old and powerful will avoid them. What they will find is what other entities wanted them to find; false information, infernal magic, maybe it'd get interesting if they found some Bahari propaganda.They could civil war within a civil war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T02:02:48-07:00","id":1401303,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> You're right, but it's something that can easily be forgotten or let to slide depending on your ST or group.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking more about the descriptions of the Sabbat in the books published so far and I don't think they represent a new departure when you take into account whose PoV those snippets come from.It's pretty standard Camarilla person sees the Sabbat in action for the first time thing isn't it?<br /> <br /> I imagine that what gets focussed on in any Sabbat book will be those who a, survived the Inquisition better and b, who remained behind in old domains. I'm less sure about b, but I don't see why you'd publish a war in the Middle East supplement for your game unless you're going for a demographic I want no part in.<br /> <br /> Part a, allows the developers to get rid of any factions they hate (please be the True Hand, please be the True hand) or don't fit in. Part b, well, who stayed behind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26282-lacheur","name":"Lacheur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T02:23:08-07:00","id":1401305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401140#post1401140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I say that the Sabbat should be reinvisioned as a non-crappy version of the True Hand.<br /> <br /> Focus on the occult, mystical, demonic part of the sect.<br /> <br /> More Montreal ceremonies in the woods.<br /> <br /> Less slaughter-maim-destroyer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mystical yes...but have the inquisition actually be successful/the infernalists realise the Anarchs are more vulnerable to them, the 'freedom loving Sabbat' who jumped to the anarchs actually be most of the sects devil worshippers, with another chunk having gone to the Cam with the Lasombra, and suddenly you spread about the Enemy Within feeling, and add a new over arching doom to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T04:16:31-07:00","id":1401315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401305#post1401305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mystical yes...but have the inquisition actually be successful/the infernalists realise the Anarchs are more vulnerable to them, the 'freedom loving Sabbat' who jumped to the anarchs actually be most of the sects devil worshippers, with another chunk having gone to the Cam with the Lasombra, and suddenly you spread about the Enemy Within feeling, and add a new over arching doom to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's silly. The Anarchs are too dumb to have the ritualist knowledge to summon demons. The only ones who are smart enough are the Setites and they know better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T04:28:01-07:00","id":1401317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401315#post1401315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's silly. The Anarchs are too dumb to have the ritualist knowledge to summon demons. The only ones who are smart enough are the Setites and they know better.</div> </div> </div> </div>*cough* House Carna *cough* besides, looking at Montreal etc, Infernalists have plenty of idiot cultists to throw to the wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T04:42:45-07:00","id":1401318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401317#post1401317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *cough* House Carna *cough* besides, looking at Montreal etc, Infernalists have plenty of idiot cultists to throw to the wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, House Ipsissimus. House Carna was planning on defecting to the Anarchs but 90% of their reason went up in flames. Now it's kind of a dual-membership house.<br /> <br /> But yes, I've always felt the Sabbat had a big infernalism &quot;problem&quot; (though I think they're overrated as a threat--infernalism is a tool that a TRUE vampire should not feel) but that was because they had a bunch of very intelligent people along with some very dumb people.<br /> <br /> As the joke at my table goes, &quot;What do you call an infernalist too smart for demons?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A Koldun.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avat