:0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T07:50:20-07:00","id":1401341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401334#post1401334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, it's not the damnation that's the issue, it's the servitude and split loyalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>ALL HAIL THE DEMON BEST'PONY!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T10:39:40-07:00","id":1401368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401336#post1401336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> what about a young fool who has magic resistance? :/<br /> <br /> also, they do offer exclusive benefits <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Demonic_Investment\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Demonic_Investment </a><br /> these don't include Devil's due investments (also check investments from Daimonion)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't say they are worse, but sabbat don't create diseases and don't syphon souls to Hell,<br /> hell, they don't even use attomic bombs or spirit nukes...hmm<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Somehow, I feel like Magic resistance would be innate to very non-magical people. The sorcery equivelent to fairy Banality if you will. But as it doesn't explicitly say that, and you're likely to put that in the headcanon box, I think it's likely that demons could remove magic resistance with an investiture. The most important thing to note, however, is that magic resistance is a very rare merit and unlikely to be of importance in the grand scheme of things. <br /> <br /> As for Demonic investments<br /> So like, every book that mentions them has a different system for them. I've made my own little meta-analysis. <br /> <br /> <b>Answer one</b>: Diamonion 6 can basically do all of that. Just buy it again and again. Personally I feel Diamonion7+ should just be more impressive Diamonion 6 powers or -become a demon and give people investments whilst harvesting worship- Similar disciplines, like Spiritus and Valeren and if we push a little; Protean, Could also endow the vampire with investment-like effects at levels 6+<br /> In 1e, Diamonion and a bunch of other &quot;infernal&quot; disciplines were granted by demons. Later on, after they dropped a bunch of those disciplines from canon, it seems to be implied that DT is something demons grant and Diamonion is just a vampiric discipline cultivated by those with a lot of infernal contact. I imagine you can develop it by feeding from thralls and demonically tainted people. Of course, Baali are a little charged for their satanism so in some books they're perfectly normal vampires who are close to the infernal and in other books they're the nephandi of vampires. V5 should hopefully set straight that Diamonion as something you learn just from drinking the right kind of blood. (but then again V5 won't have Diamonion 6 so...) <br /> <br /> <b>Answer two:</b> This might be kinda cheating because you're using the demon still. <br /> Bind the Demon.<br /> Learn the spells, Learn it's true name, kill it's thralls, command it to serve you, force it into a pretty rock that you'll hide away when you're done with it. It takes a lot of effort to do this rather than just create a normal pact. But it seems to be the case that you can control a demon and then force it to grant you investments. This is of course, highly dangerous because it can go wrong as that demon you've bound so wishes to turn the table on you. The important thing is that you don't become a thrall and get the investments you want. The downside is that you're going to be pretty paranoid (also you probably spent about half a decade of your life to achieve this thing and, player wise, put some precious points into <b>Demonology</b>)<br /> <br /> Looking at all the different DT stuff, I'm gonna go out on a limb and say the best system is to just to put powers into levels and offer them at 3x level... by no coincidence is this exactly like werewolf.... (But perhaps offer discounts if they wanna disfigure themselves for powers) <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(Dark Thaumaturgy, by the way, I'm just gonna throw it out their that I think you can learn those paths, it's just few do because they're pretty sick, people don't like recording them, and they are so heavily associated with infernalism) </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T12:30:16-07:00","id":1401382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401368#post1401368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Somehow, I feel like Magic resistance would be innate to very non-magical people. The sorcery equivelent to fairy Banality if you will. But as it doesn't explicitly say that, and you're likely to put that in the headcanon box, I think it's likely that demons could remove magic resistance with an investiture. The most important thing to note, however, is that magic resistance is a very rare merit and unlikely to be of importance in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> As for Demonic investments<br /> So like, every book that mentions them has a different system for them. I've made my own little meta-analysis.<br /> <br /> <b>Answer one</b>: Diamonion 6 can basically do all of that. Just buy it again and again. Personally I feel Diamonion7+ should just be more impressive Diamonion 6 powers or -become a demon and give people investments whilst harvesting worship- Similar disciplines, like Spiritus and Valeren and if we push a little; Protean, Could also endow the vampire with investment-like effects at levels 6+<br /> In 1e, Diamonion and a bunch of other &quot;infernal&quot; disciplines were granted by demons. Later on, after they dropped a bunch of those disciplines from canon, it seems to be implied that DT is something demons grant and Diamonion is just a vampiric discipline cultivated by those with a lot of infernal contact. I imagine you can develop it by feeding from thralls and demonically tainted people. Of course, Baali are a little charged for their satanism so in some books they're perfectly normal vampires who are close to the infernal and in other books they're the nephandi of vampires. V5 should hopefully set straight that Diamonion as something you learn just from drinking the right kind of blood. (but then again V5 won't have Diamonion 6 so...)<br /> <br /> <b>Answer two:</b> This might be kinda cheating because you're using the demon still.<br /> Bind the Demon.<br /> Learn the spells, Learn it's true name, kill it's thralls, command it to serve you, force it into a pretty rock that you'll hide away when you're done with it. It takes a lot of effort to do this rather than just create a normal pact. But it seems to be the case that you can control a demon and then force it to grant you investments. This is of course, highly dangerous because it can go wrong as that demon you've bound so wishes to turn the table on you. The important thing is that you don't become a thrall and get the investments you want. The downside is that you're going to be pretty paranoid (also you probably spent about half a decade of your life to achieve this thing and, player wise, put some precious points into <b>Demonology</b>)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree on everything except Daimonion 6, since it still counts as an investment and you still pay the price for being granted the power<br /> <br /> but even if we disregard that, the fact remains that apart from the koldun and abyss mystics, sabbat don't practice daimonion nor demonology on a regular basis,<br /> and that's...curious?<br /> <br /> daimonion is nowhere to be seen,<br /> mysticism is held exclusively by the lasombra, and even among their ranks, it's a niche practice due to it being dangerous,<br /> <br /> that leaves koldunism,<br /> but while Revised made koldunism more accessible (I assume, even to non-Tzimisce), it was still not a mainstream parctice,<br /> and even Tzimisce koldun had trouble learning the different paths<br /> <br /> I always saw it as a flawed design,<br /> just look at say Devil-Tigers, practicing the demonic arts regularly, without stigma, why is the sabbat not doing the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T12:55:50-07:00","id":1401384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401382#post1401382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I always saw it as a flawed design,<br /> just look at say Devil-Tigers, practicing the demonic arts regularly, without stigma, why is the sabbat not doing the same?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because the Demons the Sabbat have encountered seek to subvert and enslave the idiots who summon them (and the whole Sword of Caine thing, where they are really close to worshipping Caine and themselves as Vampires) Infernalism binds you to a new master, which is (Supposedly) anathema,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T13:20:35-07:00","id":1401388,"title":"","content":"DAV20, for all it's faults, has a good Daimonion writup. would recomend. The thing to read between the lines is thus; is getting 'investments' as a level 6 power the same thing as getting investments from a normal bargain? of course not. Level 6 Daimonion is when you invest in yourself; you have cultivated your own infernal power, you aren't selling your soul to any demon. You hold your own leash. The issue is it's a whole lot slower to do this than it is to deal with a demon. <br /> <br /> -----------<br /> I put infernalists in every sect. The young seek demons in their desperation to get a leg up on the old, the old have demons because they were young once. That's the biggest issue with infernalism; like diablerie, diabolism enables the young to rise up. And so the sabbat purge it from their neonates. <br /> There's a moral argument in there too but it's mostly about power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T15:51:24-07:00","id":1401407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401318#post1401318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, I've always felt the Sabbat had a big infernalism &quot;problem&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s been canonical from the beginning. It\u2019s not for nothing that they developed an internal inquisition to deal with it. It turns out that all this play-acting at Satanism and witchery (because it freaks out the normies) is a bit of a gateway drug, and not all the initiates appreciate the subtle difference between run-of-the-mill Sabbat performative edgelordism and we-actually-mean-it infernalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T20:20:58-07:00","id":1401607,"title":"","content":"Pass me the vaulderie bowl! Pass me the vaulderie bowl!<br /> <br /> I would anticipate a book much like the Anarch and Camarilla books, mostly story artifacts told from the Cainites of the sect about its current state, the conflicts and alluding to the events occurring in the current Gehenna War. I think it requires a wee bit more crunch, since the &quot;default&quot; of most settings is Camarilla and Anarch.The Sabbat will need a bit more detail, with mechanics for their rituals, lore sheets and so forth. I think this book would require more chronicle advice, such as detailing &quot;Sabbat Chronicle Tenets&quot; and conviction 'set's appropriate to how the Sabbat explore what it means to be a vampire. Perhaps the &quot;paths&quot; will be re-invented as sub-sects within the sect? Perhaps with lore sheets to chose thematically appropriate benefits? I hope there's specific tie-ins to other published sources through those artifacts- such as the Sabbat in the Chicago region- &quot;The Seven Fires.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","user":"Ruthven","date":". 07-07-2020, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T09:43:37-07:00","id":1401924,"title":"","content":"Have we heard anything about the Kiasyd? Are they still with the Sabbat? From what I remember they never really fit in with the sect and were Sabbat only because the Lasombra were Sabbat. Since th e Lasombra joined the Camarilla, is it possible the Kiasyd joined them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T09:49:44-07:00","id":1401926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401924#post1401924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we heard anything about the Kiasyd? Are they still with the Sabbat? From what I remember they never really fit in with the sect and were Sabbat only because the Lasombra were Sabbat. Since th e Lasombra joined the Camarilla, is it possible the Kiasyd joined them?</div> </div> </div> </div>most likely,<br /> since the new sabbat environment is not favorable for scholars and research (I weep for all the labs, libraries and relics the sabbat had to give up to the camarilla)<br /> <br /> that's, if they didn't get retconed, which is even more likely (they kinda retconned the harbingers and samedi already)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T09:54:18-07:00","id":1401928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1401924#post1401924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we heard anything about the Kiasyd? Are they still with the Sabbat? From what I remember they never really fit in with the sect and were Sabbat only because the Lasombra were Sabbat. Since th e Lasombra joined the Camarilla, is it possible the Kiasyd joined them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some probably joined the Camarilla but half of the Lasombra stayed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T09:57:09-07:00","id":1401929,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Kiasyd just stayed in their homes and shoed away the noise outside. <br /> <br /> Considering Obtenebration and Necromancy is one discipline they do get to say 'aha, we practiced both for a reason!' but then they'll break down crying because both powers are weaker and being good at one sacrifices being good at the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T16:40:53-07:00","id":1401989,"title":"","content":"Perhaps, with the Camarilla now becoming more secretive, the Sabbat won't actually know so much about them. I remember how, in the Sabbat Player's Guide, it was mentioned how the Sabbat only has a vague idea about what the Camarilla does and wants. Yet it never came across like that; they seemed to have a fairly good idea as well as a very low opinion of the sect. One that the Cam books themselves seemed to share at times. It's one thing to _tell_ your readers the Sabbat believe the Camarilla to be serving the Antediluvians, it's another thing to _show_ how that manifests.<br /> <br /> That may have been a byproduct of the Camarilla never really doing anything at all, granted.<br /> <br /> A bit like how both books used to tell us about how the Camarilla has, on average, more powerful blood and more Elders of great age, yet the Sabbat example characters are filled with seventh to sixth generation Elders while the one truly formidable example on the Cam side is the Malkavian Justicar(!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T01:52:50-07:00","id":1402026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering Obtenebration and Necromancy is one discipline they do get to say 'aha, we practiced both for a reason!' but then they'll break down crying because both powers are weaker and being good at one sacrifices being good at the other. </div> </div> </div>I mean, Necromancy is really about the rituals anyway so I really can't see why they can't be good with both Obtenebration and Necromancy.<br /> I wonder what will be the new Mytherceria, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T05:09:18-07:00","id":1402046,"title":"","content":"I would like to see the Sabbat go to being decentralized, the primary nucleus being the pack. I want to see the Creation Rites brought back from 2E, where EVERYONE gets buried, not just shovelheads. I'd like to see the core Auctoritas Ritae trimmed down (Creation Rites, Fire Dance, Games of Instinct, Monomacy, Vaulderie, maybe one or two more), with the Ignoblis Ritae One of My Tribe (V20 Rites of Blood) being elevated to Auctoritas because it mystically severes your Clan connection. Aside from converts, I'd also like to see majority of Sabbat being Embraced with blood of the pack.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Sabbat becoming more like the Black Hand/Lost Tribe. With the Gehenna Crusade going on, pilgrimage to the Weeping Stone can be the new thing that makes you True Sabbat. While I liked some of the changes revised made to Sabbat, I want to see them go back in some of the direction of 2E; inhuman monsters that really believed they were fighting a war against the Ancients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T08:28:12-07:00","id":1402072,"title":"","content":"I'd be on board with that. I don't think anyone is going to be completely happy with what happens with the Sabbat but as long as changes make sense given what we've been presented so far then I'm not going to complain too much. And what PJ has presented would fit. Especially the decentralized part given the decapitation of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of a haj to the weeping stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26282-lacheur","name":"Lacheur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T09:20:04-07:00","id":1402076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitenshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1402026#post1402026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, Necromancy is really about the rituals anyway so I really can't see why they can't be good with both Obtenebration and Necromancy.<br /> I wonder what will be the new Mytherceria, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/evrlly/oblivion_chart_v5/\" target=\"_blank\">As written</a>, specific Oblivion powers are required for each ritual or Ceremony. For example, the ritual to summon a ghost requires the power to identify a fetish, which itself requires one dot of Auspex. So a Kiasyd, or any Lasombra or Hecata for that matter, could theoretically be good at Obtenebration <i>or</i> Necromancy or have limited ability with both. Ceremonies need to be taught, which makes them much more accessible to Hecata (except for Abyssal Ceremonies), although I should think that Kiasyd would be more likely to have that advantage than most Lasombra, given that obscure occult research is almost all of what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T09:26:08-07:00","id":1402079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitenshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1402026#post1402026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, Necromancy is really about the rituals anyway so I really can't see why they can't be good with both Obtenebration and Necromancy.<br /> I wonder what will be the new Mytherceria, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think so? I looked at it and decided it was just as path based as thaumaturgy. Communing with the dead, Raising corpses, entering the underworld... All path magic. All that important stuff was path magic although yeah, you could consign some of those paths as rituals because they were sometimes pretty ritual like. I'll admit that I'm opposed to doing this with necromancy because I'm way more opposed to doing this with thaumaturgy and their systems are rather similar (moving one would move another) but In a vacume i'd probably be OK with it. That said, I do not like what I've seen of Oblivion so far. <br /> <br /> Mytherceria.... it'd probably be lumped into Auspex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T09:30:55-07:00","id":1402080,"title":"","content":"I really wonder what the Sabbat could look like in V5. I really think the Camarilla and the Anarchs are two sides of the same coin (the establishment vs the revolution). So, the authors should find a way to clearly separate The Sabbat from the two other Sects in order to have a proper Camarilla vs Anarchs vs Sabbat that is thematically coherent. For that, I guess they need to figure out what they want the Sabbat to be about in this edition, so that it's not &quot;the Camarilla but different&quot; or &quot;the Anarchs but different&quot;.<br /> <br /> I see two directions, which are not necessarily exclusive. The Sabbat as religious institution (just like the Camarilla is about political power). An objection I sometimes see for that is that Camarilla has cults in it now and so it stole the religious aspect of the Sabbat. But I don't necessarily think that's an issue because the Camarilla can be secular and have religion within it, just like real world countries can have secular institutions and yet, having religious people and institutions. I guess the ideology of the Sabbat still makes it at odds with the Camarilla and I can see the Anarchs wanting to fight against it.<br /> Also, there is the Sabbat as monsters. I think this part is fondamental for the identity of the Sect but I guess it implies to change the Morality system in order to make inhumane monsters a viable option for players. Either by reintroducing Paths of Enlightenment or otherwise. I don't have strong feelings about Paths but I'm not sure it's a good system to simulate inhumanity (among other things because it forces Humanity as just another Path instead of being its own thing) but I may be alone on that.<br /> <br /> So I guess my take on the Sabbat would be that Conservatives rules it, now? I think V5 goes for more decentralized factions, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T01:52:59-07:00","id":1403356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1400765#post1400765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on Sabbat Speculation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a 'mind the gap' chronicle detailing the changes to the Sabbat between V20 and V5.<br /> <br /> Civil war, beckoning, antidiluvian hunting etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not want the Gehenna War to be something that took place entirely off stage and in the past, at all, at all. It deserves at least a standalone chronicle product like the Transylvania/Ventrue/Giovanni Chronicles. At least.<br /> <br /> Catching up late to this thread, the idea of diablerie always carrying a risk of at least some form of possession pleases me for aesthetic reasons - even if it's just being haunted by a voice if the victim was weaker than the diablerist. If what gets devoured is the soul, the soul should be eternal. It should be capable of being trapped until the diablerist meets Final Death, sure, but the idea of a mere vampire destroying something that divine doesn't gel with the rest of the game line's mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 07-19-2020, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T15:49:03-07:00","id":1403426,"title":"","content":"Let me break diablerie down<br /> <br /> Goals I think we can agree on:<br /> 1 Characters AND players who commit diablerie should want to do it again for that &quot;this is addicting&quot; experience<br /> 2 Single Diableries should not unbalance the party in the long run.<br /> 3 Acquiring a low generation should be a desirable goal; ambition should be encouraged.<br /> 4 Diablerie should Horrify without breaking any of the above tennets<br /> <br /> I've gotta say, V5 doesn't do any of these well:<br /> 1- Diablerie gets worse the more you do it, as the good and bad is dependent on, and subtracts from, your humanity.<br /> 2- Based on luck, High amounts of XP are gained for successful diablerist players, unbalancing parties.<br /> 3- Low generation has many new disadvantages, such as a narrowed food choice, I would argue that a Vampire in V5 should be content with their lot in life and just accept what they were embraced with.<br /> <br /> Thus, to meet these goals, the most broadly appealing system would be as follows:<br /> <br /> -A Diablerist should gain Temporary disciplines after they diablerise, to excite the player. (1) they should not gain permanent dots (1,2)*<br /> -The Humanity loss for Diablerie should be rolled rather than automatic (1,3) which makes diablerie a gamble you can take again and again even at humanity 1 (1,3,4)<br /> -Generation should only concern how much blood you have and can use (3) A side effect of this is that if one player gets too far ahead of others, they can embrace snacks for other players so that the other players can catch up (2, 4)<br /> -Players should start in the 13-10th generation range (2, 3)<br /> -The primary problem with Diablerie should be the social fallout (4) and short term effects (erie pressence, black aura marks) that drive this problem and set diablerists against mainstream society for as long as problems persist(1,2,3,4)<br /> <br /> *Granting players very small amounts of xp for disciplines might be acceptable in otherwise high-xp games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> concerning possession if you really want to do it:<br /> Really, I think this should be limited to Vampires with Garbage willpower consuming vampires with formidable willpower. Hypothetical chart of excess willpower:<br /> x- You meet or exceed victim's willpower: They go quietly<br /> 1- you dream of a few vague memories of your victim that never truly become your own for few days.<br /> 2- You have a good amount of dream-like memories from your victim, which might be confusing for a week or so.<br /> 3-The victim's experiences will influence you to a degree depending on your willpower (2 Vs 5 will be more dramatic than 6 vs 9) for a duration of Diablerie's erie presence. This influence is not malicious or resentful (because the victim is not conscious inside you) it's merely a side effect.<br /> 4- influence lasts as long as the black marks.<br /> 5+ Victim's conscience is awake, Possession contests are made.<br /> <br /> This is good for 1 and 4 (2 isn't touched upon, 3 is subjective because you might actually like the experience of another's memories) The Temporary nature gives horror and makes metaphysical sense but isn't so long lasting or severe as to discourage diablerie (at worst, you just choose your targets better) Personally I think possession works better as hearsay/propaganda/what happens when low level suckers bite off way too much vampire, not something you get when a 13th gen brujah eats a 12th gen Tremere </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-18-2020, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T06:02:47-07:00","id":1403516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1403426#post1403426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me break diablerie down<br /> <br /> Goals I think we can agree on:<br /> 1 Characters AND players who commit diablerie should want to do it again for that &quot;this is addicting&quot; experience<br /> 2 Single Diableries should not unbalance the party in the long run.<br /> 3 Acquiring a low generation should be a desirable goal; ambition should be encouraged.<br /> 4 Diablerie should Horrify without breaking any of the above tennets<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid that no we can't &quot;agree&quot; an any of your points.<br /> <br /> 1. &quot;Wanting&quot; and &quot;addiction&quot; are two very different things. And in game diablerie is not addictive UNLESS you gain the appropriate disadvantages. In my experience as a storyteller and as a player those &quot;addicted&quot; to diablerie are a certain specific group of players desperate for &quot;levelling up&quot; in a game where the concept does not even exist. Strangely enough these are the same players who actively search for shortcuts to more power in other RPGs and tend to skrew up their fellow players when it comes to gaining mopre power for themselves (the usual justification? &quot;I'm only playing my character!&quot;).<br /> 2. Unless you plan to ask your storyteller to give &quot;the party&quot; (it's called &quot;coterie&quot; but the D&amp;D lingo works well for this kind of discussion I guess) a lot of potential low generation &quot;targets&quot; diablerie is going to unballance play, period, because no matter how you try to sell it, lower generation means more power and one player haveing more power than others is not going to work well in most games, which by the way is pretty clearly what you want to accomplish.<br /> 3. Actively acquiring low generation should be a desirable goal for some PCs, the antisocial power hungry murderhoboing kind to be precise and no, ambition shouldn't be encouraged when it entails killing and devouring souls for the sole purpose of gaining more power. <b>On the contrary, it's something that should carry an high price</b>, which seems to me is what you reject with your incessant bickering about V5 &quot;not being VtM&quot; and all your arguments summing up to &quot;I want more power and an easy way to get away with it&quot;.<br /> 4. It should horrify for sure but that's pretty difficult to accomplish when the players actively pursuing the deed for power<br /> <br /> Diablerie is one element in a vampire game, a potent one if done well. It's rare, forbidden, NEVER EASY and carries an HIGH COST. I've had players wanting to commit diablerie because they saw it as a shortcut for increasing their power but when they realized the drawbacks I was redy to enforce they had a change of heart. I did not tell them &quot;it's something you should not do&quot; but rather &quot;it's something that you've better do in an extremely smart way or not at all because if you do and you get caught you are going to pay&quot; and since in my games actions matter and have consequences they decided that hunting down and murdering a primogen or two because of their blood was not that great of an idea after all. Had they decided to do it anyway I would have crafted a story but it would not have been about power and success would have been rather difficult to achieve (I'm a fervent believer that elders are never easy to take down, especially not for satisfying power gamers), the reward would have been there but also the consequences. I would never have allowed the game to devolve in something like &quot;we go meet the primogen, murder him and suck him dry...&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T07:19:55-07:00","id":1403522,"title":"","content":"Consider the belivability of your setting: why would diablerists exist and be feared if eating a person is badWrongAwfulNo-good and everyone who partakes it immediately regrets it and vows to never do it again? <br /> <br /> On my use of the word 'party' rather than Coterie: If English isn't your native language, that's fine; but... Party is a correct term, you aren't doing anyone favours with that diatribe. <br /> <br /> Also, yeah, Vampire's literally do see diablerie as leveling up. Generations exist, dude. Every step up the ladder brings you one closer to Caine and God. You just sound like a malicious <i>Game Master</i> loathing the prospect of your players having fun with something immoral (never mind that they're playing blood sucking parasites that should meet the sun)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T08:24:44-07:00","id":1403527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1403426#post1403426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Generation should only concern how much blood you have and can use (3) A side effect of this is that if one player gets too far ahead of others, they can embrace snacks for other players so that the other players can catch up (2, 4)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>and if they don't want to embrace snacks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T09:30:47-07:00","id":1403533,"title":"","content":"Let your imagination run wild (and land on reasonable assumptions of what your players might actually do, but then again it's unlikely that a player will be so far ahead of the others in terms of Generation if you assume they all start within the 13-10 range. If you're running a game with many player diablerists, it's also unlikely that all the victims they find will be conveniently perfect for one PC; there's a rubber band in that the players with higher generations have more oppertunity to advance than players with lower generation)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T09:32:32-07:00","id":1403534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1403522#post1403522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider the belivability of your setting: why would diablerists exist and be feared if eating a person is badWrongAwfulNo-good and everyone who partakes it immediately regrets it and vows to never do it again?<br /> <br /> On my use of the word 'party' rather than Coterie: If English isn't your native language, that's fine; but... Party is a correct term, you aren't doing anyone favours with that diatribe.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, Vampire's literally do see diablerie as leveling up. Generations exist, dude. Every step up the ladder brings you one closer to Caine and God. You just sound like a malicious <i>Game Master</i> loathing the prospect of your players having fun with something immoral (never mind that they're playing blood sucking parasites that should meet the sun)</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, because it seems to me &quot;my setting&quot; is pretty in line with what VtM preached since first ed.<br /> <br /> Diablerie is cannibalism and is a grave crime in vampire society UNLESS you have the means (and/or the smarts) to get away with it. Do diablerist exist in the setting? Yes for sure, but it's not like they have it easy. Again they have the power to keep their actions secret (a lvl 6 obfuscate power that would be a lvl 5 power in V5 and let's hope no one wins a contested auspex check and realizes they are diablerists) or they have the power to have them sanctioned as legitimate by the powers that be (&quot;Yes, I diablerized Count von Chockula, but I was forced to! He was plotting with the Sabbat to overthrow the prince so me and my friends here took matters in our own hands and suceeded stopping the nefarious plot! The prince has been informed, of course! In fact he commended our actions sanctioning the diablerie... it's a sacrifice I did for the good of us all but one that weights heavily on my conscience...&quot; - note that this implies a lot of work and gameplay where the coterie made the right moves against Count von Chockula convincing the prince to sanction their actions. It's not like they decided to diablerize an elder and the prince just said &quot;be my guests&quot;). Even so once a PC becomes known as a cannibal other vampires will start to change their attitude towards them because again, in the setting Diablerie is a crime and people who are so stupid to flaunt their preference for it don't live for long and cannot expect to be socially accepted as &quot;normal members&quot; of vampire society.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;levelling up&quot; no it's not. VtM has no &quot;levels&quot;, during play you may become richer, more skilled, stronger and have more mystical power but nothing implies you have to lower your generation to compete the game is simply not built that way. As for players wanting to have fun by diablerizing their way to Caine... sure, in theory that may work but in practice it's unrealistic in the extreme and in my experience games revolving around vampires murderhoboing their way through chronicles have a tendency to fizzle really quickly. These are games where the ST needs to give players what they want (meaning: lots of low gen vampires who exist only to be diablerized by the players) and it's not much different than games of D&amp;D where players are able to convince the DM to give them uberpowerful equipment and then they proceed to wreak the campaign.<br /> <br /> TL; DR: In the VtM setting diablerie is considered one of the gravest crimes as it implies an act of utter depravity (devouring someone's soul) AND it also causes those who are more powerful than you (and even those on your level because you are a cannibal who likes to eat your own kind) to consider you a threat. It's not impossible to accomplish but it's very risky and difficult to do so. As most of the stuff in the WoD the concept is just an excuse to have goos stories it's not something that is &quot;required to compete&quot; because you need to face tougher challenges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T09:56:01-07:00","id":1403537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1403534#post1403534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny, because it seems to me &quot;my setting&quot; is pretty in line with what VtM preached since first ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong again. &quot;diablerie is bad&quot; only came into play during the revised era. During 1e Diablerie went like this:<br /> <br /> -Eats elder-<br /> I gain a dot of generation<br /> I get dark lines in my aura<br /> I roll humanity for murder<br /> I get some temporary disciplines from elder blood. <br /> <br /> And that was it. That's far closer to what I've written than the masochism you've suggested. I want to emphasize: There was no automatic loss of humanity, you just rolled for murder, Diablerie was just an interesting form of murder. <i>Socially</i> it was suicide if you got caught doing it in the Camarilla or other nice circles, but I've never said that it wasn't.<i> I will execute diablerist players if they do so in the Camarilla without setting up a safety net first</i>. <br /> <br /> Infact a big crux of my argument was that making diablerie give you health problems kinda kills the need to make it a social no-no; because after shooting yourself in the foot who wants to shoot the other foot? It's counterproductive to execute a diablerist when she's a gibbering, regretful posterchild of why diablerie is bad. Why would the Sabbat want to do what they do when it's destroying them (trick question; the sabbat want to destroy themselves)? <br /> <br /> Finaly, diablerie is not &quot;a shortcut to power&quot;, it's long term planning. Diablerie is only a shortcut to power in editions where it grants bucket loads of XP, which sadly is the current edition. 1e did not give a bucket load of XP, it just gave a dot of Generation (and elder blood gave you temporary disciplines diablerie or not in 1e)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T11:40:30-07:00","id":1403552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1403537#post1403537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong again. &quot;diablerie is bad&quot; only came into play during the revised era. During 1e Diablerie went like this:<br /> <br /> -Eats elder-<br /> I gain a dot of generation<br /> I get dark lines in my aura<br /> I roll humanity for murder<br /> I get some temporary disciplines from elder blood.<br /> <br /> And that was it. That's far closer to what I've written than the masochism you've suggested. I want to emphasize: There was no automatic loss of humanity, you just rolled for murder, Diablerie was just an interesting form of murder. <i>Socially</i> it was suicide if you got caught doing it in the Camarilla or other nice circles, but I've never said that it wasn't.<i> I will execute diablerist players if they do so in the Camarilla without setting up a safety net first</i>.<br /> <br /> Infact a big crux of my argument was that making diablerie give you health problems kinda kills the need to make it a social no-no; because after shooting yourself in the foot who wants to shoot the other foot? It's counterproductive to execute a diablerist when she's a gibbering, regretful posterchild of why diablerie is bad. Why would the Sabbat want to do what they do when it's destroying them (trick question; the sabbat want to destroy themselves)?<br /> <br /> Finaly, diablerie is not &quot;a shortcut to power&quot;, it's long term planning. Diablerie is only a shortcut to power in editions where it grants bucket loads of XP, which sadly is the current edition. 1e did not give a bucket load of XP, it just gave a dot of Generation (and elder blood gave you temporary disciplines diablerie or not in 1e)</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to mistake mechanical workings with the background of the game, but given the &quot;quality&quot; of your arguments thus far that's not really surprising... anyway:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtM 1st ed CRB page 15</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have already mentioned the Blood Bond, which is urldertaken by drinking the Blood of another Vampire (usually one's Sire or Prince). It is known that taking the Blood of one's own Get carries no such bond, and it seems also that the Antediluvians - and those others who habitually prey on their own kind - are able to do so without creating any kind of bond or obligation. This fact, more than anything, <b>makes the practice of Diablerie (as it has come to be known) a shocking and perverted thing to the Kindred, and any vampire who is a known Diabolist may be killed out of hand ,by any who find him. The diabolist must hunt with care, for he stalks the most dangerous game in the world.</b> Doubtless some find a great exhilaration in this existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who was wrong, again?<br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> <br /> Thanks for making me spend half an hour rummaging through cardboard boxes in my attic in search for the old 1st Ed CrB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 07-19-2020, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T12:13:23-07:00","id":1403553,"title":"","content":"Whoosh. <br /> <br /> The Perils of Diablerie in 1st and 2nd edition were purely social. IE Diablerists were reviled and persecuted. However, that was as far as it went. Beyond the black marks in your aura, Diablerie was beneficial. Thematically the argument could be made that in these first editions, the players, who were meant to be rebels doing their best to punch up, were meant to topple the elders and eat the rich (or become human again, which was a more obtainable goal back then) just as their elders had toppled those that came before them. <br /> <br /> The Perils of Diablerie in Revised and V20 were social, physical and mental. Diablerie was no longer just bad for vampire society, it was now also bad for you personally. Thematically, the argument was that Vampires can only win by obtaining humanity 10 and getting the right Gehenna scenario. You shouldn't fight with the elders as you'd become like them, you should just try to be a moral vampire. <br /> <br /> Perhaps you could say the thematics shifted; 1e was more punk, revised was more gothic. 1e was Gnostic-old testament, Revised more Christian. 1e was radical, revised was reactionary... <br /> <br /> So, the short of it, is that your interpretation is in line with the later games, not the early ones. <br /> 1e Diablerie- You have improved on yourself at the expense of an elder, Elders hate you. <br /> Rev Diablerie- You just ruined your character, Elders hate you. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T16:41:15-07:00","id":1403591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1403553#post1403553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoosh.<br /> <br /> The Perils of Diablerie in 1st and 2nd edition were purely social. IE Diablerists were reviled and persecuted. However, that was as far as it went. Beyond the black marks in your aura, Diablerie was beneficial. Thematically the argument could be made that in these first editions, the players, who were meant to be rebels doing their best to punch up, were meant to topple the elders and eat the rich (or become human again, which was a more obtainable goal back then) just as their elders had toppled those that came before them.<br /> <br /> The Perils of Diablerie in Revised and V20 were social, physical and mental. Diablerie was no longer just bad for vampire society, it was now also bad for you personally. Thematically, the argument was that <u><b>Vampires can only win</b></u> by obtaining humanity 10 and getting the right Gehenna scenario. You shouldn't fight with the elders as you'd become like them, you should just try to be a moral vampire.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you could say the thematics shifted; 1e was more punk, revised was more gothic. 1e was Gnostic-old testament, Revised more Christian. 1e was radical, revised was reactionary...<br /> <br /> So, the short of it, is that your interpretation is in line with the later games, not the early ones.<br /> 1e Diablerie- You have improved on yourself at the expense of an elder, Elders hate you.<br /> Rev Diablerie- You just ruined your character, Elders hate you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I quoted the very first VtM book to prove the notion that diablerie was a crime punishable with death was a thing even back then (yep, what you call &quot;purely social perils&quot; were a bloody death sentence on diablerists...).<br /> <br /> If you want to say that <b>mechanically</b> diablerie had few drawbacks in 1st ed that's true but that's a consequence of the fact the concept of the diablerized vampire being able to take control of the diablerist if the diablerie failed was introduced in later editions and rules followed suit (because the narrative parts of the game determine its mechanical aspects...). So Mithras was diablerized but only partially so, Tremere did not really subsume Saulot's soul after all and Augustus managed to turn Cappadocius into a wraith intead of wholly consuming him, and rules for diablerie slowly adpated and changed for players as well.<br /> <br /> As for your interpretation of the thematic shifts between editions I find it flawed on the deepest possible level. Aside from the fact you can't &quot;win&quot; while playing an RPG (unless your definition of winning is &quot;having fun with your friends without ruining their fun&quot;) vampire characters can accomplish their goals and generally improve themselves in 1st ed, 2nd ed, Revised, V20 and V5... if they do things right (i.e. they play smart according to their goals). If their &quot;goal&quot; is diablerizing their way to Caine and rule the planet as blood gods then I'd say their goal is... unrealistic.<br /> <br /> Humanity 10 is NOT a way of &quot;winning the game&quot; it's an extremely difficult goal to accomplish when you are a cursed bloodsucking monster who needs to feed on the living to keep existing, and let's not forget that Humanity 10 means &quot;way more human than human&quot; (&quot;living saint&quot;) which is a pretty difficult status to keep when the whole vampiric society is based on selfishness and the abuse of those weaker than you.<br /> <br /> One last thing: I wasn't making an argument about the actual rules of diablerie but mechanically speaking the current version of diablerie is an high risk/high reward enterprise. If you manage to accomplish the deed you can get large amounts of experience you can spend to increase your disciplines but you also risk eroding your humanity really quickly. Since the act is you eating someone's soul for power it seems to me the rules manage to represent quite well what diablerie is.<br /> <br /> Note that now you get extra xp for diablerizing even vampires of an higher generation than yours but can lower generation only by diablerizing those of stronger blood, which makes it easier for &quot;politically savy&quot; vampires to diablerize to their dead heart's content with little to no repercussions (again, if they play smart, other vampires don't like cannibals for obvious reasons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 07-19-2020, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T18:41:20-07:00","id":1403607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1403591#post1403591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other vampires don't like cannibals for obvious reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless that's what their entire clan is known for then the get invited to join the Camarilla. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would as argue that you can in fact &quot;win&quot; and rpG, but that's part of a bigger discussion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T02:13:11-07:00","id":1403633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1403591#post1403591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I quoted the very first VtM book to prove the notion that diablerie was a crime punishable with death was a thing even back then (yep, what you call &quot;purely social perils&quot; were a bloody death sentence on diablerists...).<br /> <br /> If you want to say that <b>mechanically</b> diablerie had few drawbacks in 1st ed that's true but that's a consequence of the fact the concept of the diablerized vampire being able to take control of the diablerist if the diablerie failed was introduced in later editions and rules followed suit (because the narrative parts of the game determine its mechanical aspects...). So Mithras was diablerized but only partially so, Tremere did not really subsume Saulot's soul after all and Augustus managed to turn Cappadocius into a wraith intead of wholly consuming him, and rules for diablerie slowly adpated and changed for players as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you notice that these are all unfathomable ancients rather than the vampires you'll usually meet? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One last thing: I wasn't making an argument about the actual rules of diablerie but mechanically speaking the current version of diablerie is an high risk/high reward enterprise. If you manage to accomplish the deed you can get large amounts of experience you can spend to increase your disciplines but you also risk eroding your humanity really quickly. Since the act is you eating someone's soul for power it seems to me the rules manage to represent quite well what diablerie is. </div> </div> </div>The thing with eating is that you're supposed to chew... Perhaps I'm a bit sensitive, but you've made the suggestion that you're one of those GM's that instills a lot of extra, mostly fluff based penalties on diablerists. I've played with a (new) storyteller that wanted to spice up Diablerie with vast amounts of attributes, abilities and disciplines (but also had the prince, who diablerised a sabbat elder, 'have a tussel' with the consciousness of his victim) and I've played a lot more with a storyteller that gave me, in one instance, a fear of intimacy and touching people, and in another instance (where I was on a Diablerie friendly path) I was possessed to send coded warnings to my victim's packmates of my ingenious plan to stake them all during the day and have them delivered... Suffice to say I'm not a fan of storytellers taking artistic liberties with Diablerie. It's best discouraged. (also note: These three diableries were the only ones I've ever commited with my characters, and the first one wasn't my choice)<br /> <br /> The latest edition is the worst possible Diablerie system. This isn't me just hating on V5; It's just a fucking terrible system and I'd hate it if it was in any other edition.<br /> It encourages high humanity vampires to Diablerise, while it makes diablerie a low reward, incredible risk action for low humanity vampires.<br /> Generation isn't the benefit here, since low generation comes with disadvantages like losing thin blood alchemy or the ability to feed from animals. The Benefit is lots of discipline XP; It destroys party balance (Imagine the one high-humanity vampire diablerises and gets 30 xp on disciplines, and then they do so again and get an extra 25xp on disciplines, while player B Diablerises once, loses an extra 2 humanity, and knows she shouldn't do it again.<br /> <br /> Since the emphasis has gone from lowering generation and moving closer to Caine, and instead moved towards gaining experience points for disciplines, Diablerie really has moved towards &quot;becoming a quick and dirty path to power&quot; rather than something you'll eventually need to do if you want to remove the limitations of your generation. I think that's a terrible thing; It's gone from a tool granted by the heavens to provide savvy vampires with the means close the gap with ancients into the vampire equivelent of skipping some grind by paying to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T11:47:14-07:00","id":1407343,"title":"","content":"Here's what I expect:<br /> <br /> - Paths will replace chronicle tenets so that instead of having one chronicle tenet everyone follows, each PC will have their own.<br /> - Sabbat convictions will be connected to other vampires rather than humans. Or perhaps via the Vinculum. In fact, the latter would be a great idea as it's one reason why Sabbat are crazy loyal to other members of their pack. Not just because of the mutual blood bond, but because it helps them remain in control of their beast.<br /> - The new Sabbat book will be the closest to a hack and slash game that VTM ever gets. I expect it will revolve around events in the middle east and the numerous Sabbat packs heading there to fight off the 'great evil' that are ancient vampires and their cronies.<br /> - Diablerie is indeed much much harder in V5 (thank god), but given Sabbat love drinking souls, there might be a system in place, likely tied to the Vinculum or other Sabbat rituals, that could greatly reduce the risk of being taken over by the elder's soul. Note: reduced risk, not taken away entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T06:07:32-07:00","id":1407911,"title":"","content":"I know this is a bit random but why do people like the Sabbat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T06:18:07-07:00","id":1407916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1407911#post1407911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a bit random but why do people like the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div>A poem for you: <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Do not go gentle into that good night,<br /> Old age should burn and rave at close of day;<br /> Rage, rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> Though wise men at their end know dark is right,<br /> Because their words had forked no lightning they<br /> Do not go gentle into that good night.<br /> <br /> Good men, the last wave by, crying how bright<br /> Their frail deeds might have danced in a green bay,<br /> Rage, rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> Wild men who caught and sang the sun in flight,<br /> And learn, too late, they grieved it on its way,<br /> Do not go gentle into that good night.<br /> <br /> Grave men, near death, who see with blinding sight<br /> Blind eyes could blaze like meteors and be gay,<br /> Rage, rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> And you, my father, there on the sad height,<br /> Curse, bless, me now with your fierce tears, I pray.<br /> Do not go gentle into that good night.<br /> Rage, rage against the dying of the light<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Do not go gentle into that good night</b><br /> Dylan Thomas - 1914-1953</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-13-2020, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T06:28:19-07:00","id":1407917,"title":"","content":"Maybe I should've chosen Achebe, <span style=\"font-size:8px\">or the great JREG</span>; <br /> <br /> Men just want to die in a war with like minded people for a cause greater than themselves. You might live longer with the camarilla, but you're going to hate everyone there. Sabbat games also have the advantage of constant hilarity. Fascism has a certain appeal to it; that appeal is fantastical, but when you're playing a game of vampires, and that fantastical appeal is in part the reality you find yourself in, what more is there to joy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T06:47:09-07:00","id":1407923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1407916#post1407916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A poem for you: <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Do not go gentle into that good night,<br /> Old age should burn and rave at close of day;<br /> Rage, rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> Though wise men at their end know dark is right,<br /> Because their words had forked no lightning they<br /> Do not go gentle into that good night.<br /> <br /> Good men, the last wave by, crying how bright<br /> Their frail deeds might have danced in a green bay,<br /> Rage, rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> Wild men who caught and sang the sun in flight,<br /> And learn, too late, they grieved it on its way,<br /> Do not go gentle into that good night.<br /> <br /> Grave men, near death, who see with blinding sight<br /> Blind eyes could blaze like meteors and be gay,<br /> Rage, rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> And you, my father, there on the sad height,<br /> Curse, bless, me now with your fierce tears, I pray.<br /> Do not go gentle into that good night.<br /> Rage, rage against the dying of the light<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Do not go gentle into that good night</b><br /> Dylan Thomas - 1914-1953</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but the Sabbat are huge dicks about it,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T07:39:24-07:00","id":1407931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1407911#post1407911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a bit random but why do people like the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The ability to play villains or anti-heroes, basically. Monstrous creatures who sincerely believe they are that way for the greater good. Like being part of a large cult, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T07:44:05-07:00","id":1407932,"title":"","content":"L.o the Sabbat do not believe they doing stuff for the greater good, they want to lord over Kine.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is the, bad guys that think they are doing good, guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T07:48:32-07:00","id":1407935,"title":"","content":"In my head the Sabbat never 100% vanished, there were those left behind either by their own will or left behind by Sires who thought that the Middle East was more important. I don't want to see a 100% full reversal of &quot;SIKE! They never left.&quot; but I'd like to see some of it come back. It would feel strange if they all left and just all came back thinking &quot;Job done!'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storyteller of Boston by Night on Twitch <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath</a><br /> Fan of WOD Since 2013","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26354-michelleclight","name":"MichelleCLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:58:15-07:00","id":1407988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1407911#post1407911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a bit random but why do people like the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BfWF5y5LVoQ\" data-code=\"BfWF5y5LVoQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/BfWF5y5LVoQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T12:21:36-07:00","id":1407999,"title":"","content":"For me personally, here are some of the reasons I like the Sabbat:<br /> <br /> \u2022They make great antagonists - no matter what kind of vampire you\u2019re playing, the Sabbat can fuck up your shit or provide an interesting counter argument <br /> <br /> \u2022Contrast<br /> -The Sabbat are an interesting contrast to the Camarilla as a militant theocratic conspiracy rather then a conservative neo-feudal conspiracy. The Sabbat allows for exploration of mysticism, religion, and monstrosity without the restraints of the Camarilla or Anarchs - but with their own restraints of course<br /> <br /> \u2022What Could Have Been<br /> -The Sabbat are the result of a justified revolt against abusive elders and a seismic shift in nocturnal politics. They were the first Anarchs, pioneering for brotherhood and freedom from the tyranny of the elders. They are a revolution that was co-opted by counter-revolutionaries that were theocrats and politicians who cared more for their own power rather then the true ideas of the revolution and the clash between these conservative leaders and the revolutionary bodies continues to this night<br /> <br /> \u2022Fraternitas<br /> -Vampires are addicted, ruthless, amoral, sociopathic bastard who would sell their mother\u2019s for a blood bag and burn their best friend for having a nicer house then them - before moving into said house. The Camarilla and Anarchs both show this in different ways. So does the Sabbat, to be fair. However, the Sabbat is also different. Sure, bishops and priscus play the jyhad; but down at the street level? Packs care about each other - the bond might be mystically imposes but the feelings seem real. Pack mates would kill or die for one another; they fight together, they mourn together, they celebrate together. They reject the solitary hell of Caine\u2019s Curse and rejoice in each other\u2019s company and when you feel alone... that sounds pretty good. Just ask most cults.<br /> <br /> \u2022Lore<br /> -You\u2019re getting low on humanity and need a new path to survive? Find a Sabbat mystic and learn their ways. You want to know the truth of the jyhad and the secrets of Noddist lore? The Sabbat has your back - just report any torpid elders you find. After interrogation, we feast!<br /> <br /> \u2022In A Way, They\u2019re Right<br /> -The Sabbat, like all groups - particularly groups of vampires, is flawed. However, they also aren\u2019t entirely wrong. Elders do rule over their children with iron fists and without concern for the safety of the childer. Founders do rule over clans for their own eldritch purposes. The Antediluvians may well be the champions of Gehenna. The Camarilla willfully ignores the threat and most Anarchs are ignorant of it - most independent clans are actively AIDING their founders! The Sabbat are the only ones that seem to be willing to treat this like the threat it is and depending on the ST, the efforts of the Sabbat may be one of the things keeping infernalists and antediluvians at bay.<br /> <br /> \u2022Finally...<br /> -Well, like, listen, I\u2019m a normal and well-adjusted person but, I mean, come on...<br /> <br /> Sometimes I just want to be a Brujah Antitribu named \u2018Tony the Hammer\u2019 who likes to play golf with human heads, is that so wrong?!?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:10:14-07:00","id":1408060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1407999#post1407999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022In A Way, They\u2019re Right<br /> -The Sabbat, like all groups - particularly groups of vampires, is flawed. However, they also aren\u2019t entirely wrong. Elders do rule over their children with iron fists and without concern for the safety of the childer. Founders do rule over clans for their own eldritch purposes. The Antediluvians may well be the champions of Gehenna. The Camarilla willfully ignores the threat and most Anarchs are ignorant of it - most independent clans are actively AIDING their founders! The Sabbat are the only ones that seem to be willing to treat this like the threat it is and depending on the ST, the efforts of the Sabbat may be one of the things keeping infernalists and antediluvians at bay.<br /> !</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except its pretty obvious the Sabbat are as much a tool of the Jyhad as anything else. Everything they Rail against.. exists in the Sabbat. This doesn't make them any less interesting but the perspective that they are the people on the right side of Gehenna preparing to Fight off the Antedeluvians vs being another level of the game comes off as no different to me than people who argue the Camarilla isn't basically one big vampiric organized crime ring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:34:46-07:00","id":1408067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1407911#post1407911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a bit random but why do people like the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people play vampire to play tragic tortured monsters cursed by their humanity.<br /> <br /> Some people play vampire to be freed from the shackles of Dungeons and Dragons morality and instead revel in being a monster.<br /> <br /> Playing Sabbat is playing Grand Theft Auto by Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:54:15-07:00","id":1408071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408067#post1408067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some people play vampire to play tragic tortured monsters cursed by their humanity.<br /> <br /> Some people play vampire to be freed from the shackles of Dungeons and Dragons morality and instead revel in being a monster.<br /> <br /> Playing Sabbat is playing Grand Theft Auto by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are valid ways of playing. And even Sabbat Cainites can experience moral and personal dilemmas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T19:03:54-07:00","id":1408091,"title":"","content":"Oh, I ain\u2019t arguing that the Sabbat aren\u2019t corrupt to the bone.<br /> <br /> That point is simply to argue that, if an ST is interested in it, the Sabbat can be a genuine force to oppose the founders of the clan - although unfortunately most of the Sabbat\u2019s primary accomplishments in that regard... haven\u2019t really happened.<br /> <br /> Again, I won\u2019t argue that their not corrupt, but like every faction they do have their upsides. The organization is horrific, but they do have a small handful of positive traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","valu