ps://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T07:55:31-07:00","id":1408152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408095#post1408095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a theory for the Gehenna War.<br /> <br /> The reason the Lasombra jumped ship was the realization the Antediluvians were real. So they ran screaming as their cult was all about it being a scam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but isn't it the other way around? Camarilla claims they are a myth, whereas Sabbat consider themselves Caine's holy warriors against his grandchilder.<br /> <br /> I believe Lasombra jumped ship because they realized that the Sabbat were getting beaten hard by the SI and that the structure and secrecy of the Camarilla was the only way to ensure the survival of their clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:08:29-07:00","id":1408155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408152#post1408152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but isn't it the other way around? Camarilla claims they are a myth, whereas Sabbat consider themselves Caine's holy warriors against his grandchilder.</div> </div> </div> </div>in v5, the Camarilla does recognize antideluvians,<br /> <br /> not sure what Phipps is on about, he probably had some wild headcanon that Lasombra had invented the whole antideluvian thing to scam the sabbat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:10:37-07:00","id":1408157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408155#post1408155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> in v5, the Camarilla does recognize antideluvians,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm ... they do? Source and page? I have all the books, but it's possible I missed that bit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:23:48-07:00","id":1408163,"title":"","content":"In V5, the Camarilla allow open religions. <br /> (No doubt to appease their Elder-Sabbat converts who sent the young sabbat off to die) <br /> <br /> They don't actually hold a stance on antideluvians as a sect, the government is still a secular one, they just allow people to believe otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T09:26:24-07:00","id":1408176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408095#post1408095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a theory for the Gehenna War.<br /> <br /> The reason the Lasombra jumped ship was the realization the Antediluvians were real. So they ran screaming as their cult was all about it being a scam.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or, that they came to the realization that their Antedeluvian was not as dead as they thought. Alternately, they realize there are things that are perhaps scarier than the Antedeluvians. (Shalim)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:57:33-07:00","id":1408207,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26354-michelleclight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26354_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26354\" data-vbnamecard=\"26354\">MichelleCLight</a> I forgot about that scene till you mentioned it, but that was pretty intense.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24641\" data-vbnamecard=\"24641\">SarcasticJazzHands</a> what if Shalim is the Lasombra Antediluvian (who I still think was female but has now transcended gender)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T12:01:11-07:00","id":1408210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408155#post1408155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> in v5, the Camarilla does recognize antideluvians,<br /> <br /> not sure what Phipps is on about, he probably had some wild headcanon that Lasombra had invented the whole antideluvian thing to scam the sabbat</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is that Lasombra are cult leaders. They use religion to control the masses. They don't generally actually BELIEVE the same way that, say, the Followers of Set do.<br /> <br /> So the discovery that their Crusade ACTUALLY WOKE UP ANCIENTS would be terrifying to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T12:04:30-07:00","id":1408211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408210#post1408210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm saying is that Lasombra are cult leaders. They use religion to control the masses. They don't generally actually BELIEVE the same way that, say, the Followers of Set do.<br /> <br /> So the discovery that their Crusade ACTUALLY WOKE UP ANCIENTS would be terrifying to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. They did the same thing with the Catholic Church and the Cainite Heresy in medieval Europe, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T12:08:21-07:00","id":1408213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408207#post1408207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24641\" data-vbnamecard=\"24641\">SarcasticJazzHands</a> what if Shalim is the Lasombra Antediluvian (who I still think was female but has now transcended gender)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly an option. In my game, an NPC and then later a PC had their souls sucked into the Abyss and spent time there, and experienced the creature that was the sky, an unfathonable entity.<br /> <br /> They also discovered that a portion of a vampire's soul is brought to the Abyss, when they are embraced, and the PC's abyss soul shard was inhabiting her body for a time before the true soul was able to escape the Abyss and return to her body.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T13:25:25-07:00","id":1408230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408211#post1408211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. They did the same thing with the Catholic Church and the Cainite Heresy in medieval Europe, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was mostly to check the growing Venture influence in the aristocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:28:00-07:00","id":1408239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408230#post1408230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was mostly to check the growing Venture influence in the aristocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always felt the Lasombra were doing the same with the Sabbat. The Archbishops, Cardinals, and Pricuses aren't actually in charge of the Sabbat because they believe in Gehenna or FREEDOM.<br /> <br /> They're doing it because they own their own sect like they think the Ventrue do.<br /> <br /> They just use religion as a method of control and getting the flunkies to die for them. They're very much believers that Kindred religion is the opiate of the masses.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:43:13-07:00","id":1408243,"title":"","content":"I think your forgetting the the other path the Lasombra espouse which is Power and the Inner voice. Power by birthright or embrace is a Venture thing, Taking power with only your two hands and the gifts of the blood and holding it is prime Lasombra. <br /> <br /> The notion that anything the clan does is simply to one up the Venture like some childish rivalry is silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:56:08-07:00","id":1408246,"title":"","content":"I'd love it if the Sabbat were supported as anything but profoundly delusional. Yes that's &quot;up to the st&quot; but between mechanics and canonical presentaiton they are presented as Wrong about fighting the Antedeluvians. Wrong about Paths being anything but dead ends. They might style themselves as post human monsters.. but they rarely are even most of the Elders of the Sabbat come off as Low humanity vs &quot;Post human&quot;.(and the fact that they have so many damned elders says alot about their positions in and of themselves)<br /> <br /> That you'd have to find some sort of secret hermits who might teach you the ways get off the system isn't really all the different than the promises of golconda hermits for Humanity. I've never found Sabbat to play all the different than standard games AND I hope that v5 changes this. Customize the game around playing Sabbat. Sabbat have always been held back by being forced onto a chasis built for playing Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:59:18-07:00","id":1408248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3953_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3953\" data-vbnamecard=\"3953\">Dwight</a> I think you\u2019re both right about the Lasombra. Your positions are not mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:04:06-07:00","id":1408251,"title":"","content":"I think you could view the Sabbat as being vampires with more of a 'physical' emphasis - more warrior caste the way the Camarilla are the filthy politicians (more 'mental?') and the Anarchs are the workers (more 'social'- I dont know if I'm making communist puns here) In that context you've had the Sabbat 'going to war' and that's going to have consequences. CtPhipp's Crusades analogy has them bringing back (plundered) knowledge, but there can be other dimensions to it. Think of something akin to Vietnam - returning from wars, having to struggle with 're-integrating', suffering from the vampiric equivalent of PTSD, etc. Some may still be determined to wage that war, or may see new threats (ie the Second Inquisition) cropping up and then go to war<br /> against THAT new threat. You could also have a faction of the Sabbat interested in maintaining elements of the Black Hand ideology ('guarding the herd's of humanity from predation. because they see those herds as their property, for example.) <br /> <br /> An 'army' is going to need more than just the tip of the spear though. You have the officers and leadership. You have your provosts/Military police (a reimagining of the Inquisition?) you could even have your own diplomats and workers, and suchlike. The Antes may or may not still be a threat but Sabbat who 'return' from the wars can find plenty of things to face or do. They're likely to find the Camarilla and Anarchs muscling in on territory they abandoned when they went to war, so they'll have to start carving out their own niches again to reclaim territory and resources. Or perhaps some of the Sabbat are sent 'back' from the War to start establishing new bases from which supplies (and manpower) can be routed into the wars (recruiting grounds, logistics, etc.)<br /> <br /> Diablerie for this imagining of the Sabbat is likely to be a tool of intelligence and self-improvement. Learning to use the enemy's own weapons against them basically (with all the benefits and dangers that implies.) <br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it strictly 'good' or 'bad' but it depends on how its used and justified. Heck, maybe you have the concept of diablerie starting to break previous definitions (thee original material has always been kind of murky I felt... 'True' Diablerie always required consuming not just the vitae but soul of the victim. And yet there are plenty of cases where sucking the blood without consuming the soul still confers some measure of power including lowered generation. It's just a more imperfect process.) So 'Blood' Diablerie might be treated differently from 'Soul' Diablerie.<br /> There's also variations found like in thautmaturgy (the rite of the bitter rose) which opens the possibility of new ways to utilize Diablerie as part of a larger war (maybe the Sabbat develop their own synthesis of traditional thaumaturgy and thin blooded alchemy? I dunno.) Diablerie of the Soul may still be considered something to be restricted (there ARE downsides and dangers, like the soul of the victim taking over his attacker) but Blood diablerie might be more of a gray area where rules can be more safely bent and justified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T12:42:05-07:00","id":1408397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408239#post1408239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always felt the Lasombra were doing the same with the Sabbat. The Archbishops, Cardinals, and Pricuses aren't actually in charge of the Sabbat because they believe in Gehenna or FREEDOM.<br /> <br /> They're doing it because they own their own sect like they think the Ventrue do.<br /> <br /> They just use religion as a method of control and getting the flunkies to die for them. They're very much believers that Kindred religion is the opiate of the masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm starting to think that you're seeing everything through Brujah tinted glasses<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T12:53:36-07:00","id":1408399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-