don</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:02:24-07:00","id":1408478,"title":"","content":"the Sabbat is just obsolete,<br /> the Ancients they rose to fight are no longer the godlike horrors of legend, but other licks barely stronger than your average ancilla<br /> <br /> diablerie is pointless, since there's not much power to be gained from it and the risks far outweigh the benefits<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:47:28-07:00","id":1408489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408478#post1408478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Sabbat is just obsolete,<br /> the Ancients they rose to fight are no longer the godlike horrors of legend, but other licks barely stronger than your average ancilla<br /> <br /> diablerie is pointless, since there's not much power to be gained from it and the risks far outweigh the benefits</div> </div> </div> </div>Wym by the second paragraph? Are you saying they nerfed Antediluvians and Methuselahs in V5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:56:01-07:00","id":1408491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408489#post1408489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wym by the second paragraph? Are you saying they nerfed Antediluvians and Methuselahs in V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no special Discipline levels or Traits above 5 now, which is what the common complaint is. But people ignore the things in the book that make those higher BP/lower Gen characters trong enough to stomp groups of Neonates even without 'I can Dominate an entire country!' or 'I can transform into dragon!'<br /> <br /> And this is also looking at them based on the existing mechanics for the game, which are built around playing neonates and ancillae because it's a new core book meant largely for new players (V5 is the first time the game has had print since 2004, which means a new audience in general), and people are judging the entire everything based on that. We don't know what, if any, special stuff they may build in the coming development for elders and methuselahs (because playing as those don't matter in the core book), beyond the one mandate of 'no traits above 5'. .<br /> <br /> So 'nerfed' is an inaccurate word when we know literally nothing beyond 'The methuselahs in Chicago don't have special powers or traits above 5'. It's also ignoring the entire different scale of V5 in general.<br /> <br /> (Also, Antediluvians should be literal plot devices anyway, so their stats really should not matter in any way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 08-16-2020, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T07:02:42-07:00","id":1408492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408491#post1408491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are no special Discipline levels or Traits above 5 now, which is what the common complaint is. But people ignore the things in the book that make those higher BP/lower Gen characters trong enough to stomp groups of Neonates even without 'I can Dominate an entire country!' or 'I can transform into dragon!'<br /> <br /> And this is also looking at them based on the existing mechanics for the game, which are built around playing neonates and ancillae because it's a new core book meant largely for new players (V5 is the first time the game has had print since 2004, which means a new audience in general), and people are judging the entire everything based on that. We don't know what, if any, special stuff they may build in the coming development for elders and methuselahs (because playing as those don't matter in the core book), beyond the one mandate of 'no traits above 5'. .<br /> <br /> So 'nerfed' is an inaccurate word when we know literally nothing beyond 'The methuselahs in Chicago don't have special powers or traits above 5'. It's also ignoring the entire different scale of V5 in general.<br /> <br /> (Also, Antediluvians should be literal plot devices anyway, so their stats really should not matter in any way).</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules to play elders are in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T07:48:07-07:00","id":1408496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408476#post1408476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat has been secretly infiltrated by Ancients the entire time!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the sect was run by the Lasombra and Tzimisce Founders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T09:16:30-07:00","id":1408500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408496#post1408496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the sect was run by the Lasombra and Tzimisce Founders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? The Sabbat thought they devoured both the Lasombra and Tzimisce Antes (though they were wrong about the Eldest and maybe wrong about Lasombra).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T09:18:29-07:00","id":1408501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408500#post1408500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure? The Sabbat thought they devoured both the Lasombra and Tzimisce Antes (though they were wrong about the Eldest and maybe wrong about Lasombra).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they were wrong about both.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra Trilogy has Lucita visit Gratiano and realizes he's a brainwashed moron.<br /> <br /> I don't think either Antediluvian cared to run the sects, though. They have loftier goals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T09:25:41-07:00","id":1408503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408492#post1408492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rules to play elders are in the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, you can use everything in the core book to play Elders out of the gate with no problem.<br /> <br /> But there are no specific Elder rules, such as the Sea of Time for Elders. And with that, comes any potential special things that they might tweak for elder play. It's not something I really expect to have a lot of detail to, if they do any special tweaks at all, but they're not truly 'covered' by the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T09:35:04-07:00","id":1408505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408501#post1408501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they were wrong about both.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra Trilogy has Lucita visit Gratiano and realizes he's a brainwashed moron.<br /> <br /> I don't think either Antediluvian cared to run the sects, though. They have loftier goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was always my take. Each developed their own strategy to either win the Jyhad or transcend it by becoming something other than a Cainite, and they faked their deaths to avoid being distracted by their siblings' schemes.<br /> <br /> My headcanon is that the same is true of Cappadocius, Saulot, and Malkav.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T09:57:43-07:00","id":1408506,"title":"","content":"I find the antedulivians escaping diablerie tiresome, but it works for Tzmisce and Lasombra, insofar as they set up the board for their Diablerie. <br /> Saulot... now, If Saulot sired the Baali, thus setting up the board for his own Diablerie, that'd give him all the reason to possess Tremere. But if not then I don't really care for the -Saulot pulls tremere strings- plot they've got on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T10:10:26-07:00","id":1408508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408501#post1408501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they were wrong about both.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra Trilogy has Lucita visit Gratiano and realizes he's a brainwashed moron.<br /> <br /> I don't think either Antediluvian cared to run the sects, though. They have loftier goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Idk that.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I agree.<br /> <br /> What about Troile?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T10:21:52-07:00","id":1408510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408506#post1408506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the antedulivians escaping diablerie tiresome, but it works for Tzmisce and Lasombra, insofar as they set up the board for their Diablerie.<br /> Saulot... now, If Saulot sired the Baali, thus setting up the board for his own Diablerie, that'd give him all the reason to possess Tremere. But if not then I don't really care for the -Saulot pulls tremere strings- plot they've got on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That there was something &quot;off&quot; about Saulot's diab has been the case since the earliest days. That he and much of the most powerful 4th gens of the clan meekly handed themselves over for diab has always been a think and its something that completely freaked out Etrius. Clearly there was SOME sort of plan clan tremere was not let in on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T10:27:04-07:00","id":1408511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408510#post1408510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That there was something &amp;quot;off&amp;quot; about Saulot's diab has been the case since the earliest days. That he and much of the most powerful 4th gens of the clan meekly handed themselves over for diab has always been a think and its something that completely freaked out Etrius. Clearly there was SOME sort of plan clan tremere was not let in on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I please ask for a source regarding Etrius' concerns? Not challenging you, but that sounds very interesting and more details could be helpful for the plot of the chronicle I am currently running <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T10:28:01-07:00","id":1408512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400491-v5-the-official-sabbat-speculation-thread?p=1408506#post1408506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the antedulivians escaping diablerie tiresome, but it works for Tzmisce and Lasombra, insofar as they set up the board for their Diablerie.<br /> Saulot... now, If Saulot sired the Baali, thus setting up the board for his own Diablerie, that'd give him all the reason to possess Tremere. But if not then I don't really care for the -Saulot pulls tremere strings- plot they've got on.</div> </div> </div> </div>saulot had Obeah 9, he was virtually safe from diablerie<br /> <br /> salubri usually let themselves be diablerised after reaching golconda to free their souls,<br /> I'm not sure if it's a golconda thing or an obeah 9 thing<br /> <br /> Cappadocius (who was friends with saulot) also supposedly reached golconda and let itself be diablerise to free its soul<br /> <br /> <br /> whatever the case, these topics about antideluvians are pointless and unproductive,<br /> I'm not talking about them, I'm talking about stated ancients that are covered by mechanics,<br /> antideluvians have their uses, but they make for very poor games/plot devices as shown by the Gehenna book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T12:41:36-07:00","id":1408540,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> I\u2019ve never compared Helena in CbN 5e with her character in the original CbN. Is she a lot less powerful in V5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":